#: src/features/RolePlay/scenarios/hotel-check-in.ts:13
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid ""
"Checking into a hotel usually follows a predictable pattern. The "
"receptionist confirms your identity and reservation, explains the hotel’s "
"services, and gives you access to your room.\n"
"\n"
"Knowing a few key phrases can make the process much easier, especially when "
"you are travelling in a country where you do not speak the local language "
"confidently.\n"
"\n"
"## What You May Need at Check-In\n"
"\n"
"The receptionist may ask you for:\n"
"\n"
"- Your full name\n"
"- A passport or identity document\n"
"- Your booking confirmation\n"
"- A payment card\n"
"- The number of guests\n"
"- Your expected check-out date\n"
"\n"
"You can begin the conversation with:\n"
"\n"
"- “Hello, I have a reservation.”\n"
"- “Hi, I’d like to check in.”\n"
"- “The reservation should be under Alex Dmowski.”\n"
"- “I booked the room through a booking website.”\n"
"- “Here is my booking confirmation.”\n"
"\n"
"If the receptionist cannot find your reservation, stay calm and provide "
"more details:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could you check the booking number?”\n"
"- “I received a confirmation email yesterday.”\n"
"- “The reservation may be under my partner’s name.”\n"
"- “Would it help if I showed you the confirmation?”\n"
"\n"
"## Confirm the Important Details\n"
"\n"
"Before accepting the room, confirm that the reservation details are "
"correct.\n"
"\n"
"You may want to check:\n"
"\n"
"- The room type\n"
"- The number of nights\n"
"- The total price\n"
"- Whether breakfast is included\n"
"- The number and size of beds\n"
"- The check-out time\n"
"- Any additional fees or deposits\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could you confirm which room type I booked?”\n"
"- “Is breakfast included in the price?”\n"
"- “What time is check-out?”\n"
"- “Is there a security deposit?”\n"
"- “Are there any additional charges?”\n"
"- “Has the room already been paid for?”\n"
"- “Could I have a receipt, please?”\n"
"\n"
"Do not be afraid to ask the receptionist to repeat information:\n"
"\n"
"- “Sorry, could you repeat that?”\n"
"- “Could you speak a little more slowly, please?”\n"
"- “Did you say check-out is at eleven?”\n"
"- “Could you write that down for me?”\n"
"\n"
"## Ask About Hotel Services\n"
"\n"
"Check-in is a good time to ask practical questions about your stay.\n"
"\n"
"### Wi-Fi\n"
"\n"
"- “Is Wi-Fi included?”\n"
"- “What is the Wi-Fi password?”\n"
"- “Does the Wi-Fi work inside the rooms?”\n"
"\n"
"### Breakfast\n"
"\n"
"- “What time is breakfast served?”\n"
"- “Where is the breakfast area?”\n"
"- “Do you have vegetarian options?”\n"
"- “Can I add breakfast to my reservation?”\n"
"\n"
"### Hotel facilities\n"
"\n"
"- “Does the hotel have a gym?”\n"
"- “Is there a place where I can leave my luggage?”\n"
"- “Do you have laundry service?”\n"
"- “Is room service available?”\n"
"- “Is there a restaurant in the hotel?”\n"
"\n"
"### Transport and local information\n"
"\n"
"- “Could you help me call a taxi?”\n"
"- “What is the easiest way to get to the city centre?”\n"
"- “Is there a bus stop nearby?”\n"
"- “Could you recommend a restaurant in the area?”\n"
"\n"
"## Make a Special Request\n"
"\n"
"It is best to make important requests before arriving, but you can also ask "
"at reception.\n"
"\n"
"Common requests include:\n"
"\n"
"- A quiet room\n"
"- A room on a higher or lower floor\n"
"- Two separate beds\n"
"- A larger bed\n"
"- A baby cot\n"
"- An accessible room\n"
"- Extra towels or pillows\n"
"- Early check-in\n"
"- Late check-out\n"
"- A room away from the lift\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases:\n"
"\n"
"- “Would it be possible to have a quiet room?”\n"
"- “Could I have a room away from the lift?”\n"
"- “Do you have a room on a higher floor?”\n"
"- “Could we have two separate beds?”\n"
"- “Would it be possible to check out later?”\n"
"- “Could you send an extra towel to the room?”\n"
"\n"
"Using “Could I…?”, “Would it be possible…?” and “Do you have…?” makes your "
"request sound polite and natural.\n"
"\n"
"## Handle Common Problems\n"
"\n"
"Sometimes the room is not ready, the booking details are incorrect, or the "
"room does not match what you reserved.\n"
"\n"
"### The room is not ready\n"
"\n"
"- “Do you know when the room will be ready?”\n"
"- “Could I leave my luggage here?”\n"
"- “Could you let me know when I can check in?”\n"
"- “Is there somewhere I can wait?”\n"
"\n"
"### The reservation cannot be found\n"
"\n"
"- “I have a confirmation email. Could you check it?”\n"
"- “Could you search using the booking reference?”\n"
"- “The reservation may be under a different name.”\n"
"- “Could you contact the booking platform?”\n"
"\n"
"### The room is different from the booking\n"
"\n"
"- “I believe I booked a double room.”\n"
"- “My confirmation says that breakfast is included.”\n"
"- “I requested two separate beds.”\n"
"- “Could you check the original reservation?”\n"
"- “Is another room available?”\n"
"\n"
"### There is a problem with the room\n"
"\n"
"- “The air conditioning does not seem to work.”\n"
"- “The room has not been cleaned yet.”\n"
"- “There is a lot of noise coming from the next room.”\n"
"- “The Wi-Fi is not working in my room.”\n"
"- “Could someone take a look at it?”\n"
"- “Would it be possible to change rooms?”\n"
"\n"
"Describe the problem clearly, explain what you expected, and ask for a "
"specific solution.\n"
"\n"
"## Understand Common Receptionist Questions\n"
"\n"
"A receptionist may ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “May I have your name?”\n"
"- “Could I see your passport or ID?”\n"
"- “Do you have your booking confirmation?”\n"
"- “How many nights will you be staying?”\n"
"- “Will you be paying by card or cash?”\n"
"- “Would you like breakfast included?”\n"
"- “Do you need help with your luggage?”\n"
"- “Would you like a wake-up call?”\n"
"- “Do you have any special requests?”\n"
"\n"
"You do not need to give long answers. Clear and direct responses are "
"usually best.\n"
"\n"
"For example:\n"
"\n"
"> “Yes, the reservation is under Dmowski. I’ll be staying for three nights, "
"and I’ll pay by card.”\n"
"\n"
"## A Simple Check-In Conversation\n"
"\n"
"A typical conversation may follow this structure:\n"
"\n"
"1. Greet the receptionist.\n"
"2. Say that you have a reservation.\n"
"3. Give your name and identification.\n"
"4. Confirm your booking details.\n"
"5. Ask about breakfast, Wi-Fi, or check-out.\n"
"6. Make any special requests.\n"
"7. Collect your room key and directions.\n"
"8. Thank the receptionist.\n"
"\n"
"Example:\n"
"\n"
"> **Guest:** Hello, I have a reservation under Dmowski.  \n"
"> **Receptionist:** Certainly. May I see your passport, please?  \n"
"> **Guest:** Of course. Here you are. Is breakfast included in my booking?  "
"\n"
"> **Receptionist:** Yes, it is served from seven until ten.  \n"
"> **Guest:** Great. Could you also tell me the Wi-Fi password?  \n"
"> **Receptionist:** It is written on your key card.  \n"
"> **Guest:** Thank you. What time is check-out?  \n"
"> **Receptionist:** Check-out is at eleven.  \n"
"> **Guest:** Perfect. Thank you for your help.\n"
"\n"
"## Practice Scenario\n"
"\n"
"In this roleplay, you have arrived at a hotel where you already have a "
"reservation. The AI receptionist will ask for your details, explain the "
"hotel’s services, and respond to your questions.\n"
"\n"
"During the conversation, try to:\n"
"\n"
"- Introduce yourself and confirm your reservation.\n"
"- Ask at least two questions about the hotel.\n"
"- Make one polite request.\n"
"- Confirm an important detail by repeating it.\n"
"- Respond to an unexpected issue if one occurs.\n"
"\n"
"Focus on communicating clearly rather than using perfect grammar. A "
"successful check-in is one where both you and the receptionist understand "
"what needs to happen next."
msgstr ""
"Proses daftar masuk ke hotel biasanya mengikuti corak tetap. Penyambut "
"tetamu mengesahkan identiti dan tempahan anda, menerangkan perkhidmatan "
"hotel, dan memberi anda akses ke bilik anda.\n"
"\n"
"Mengetahui beberapa frasa penting boleh memudahkan proses ini, terutama "
"apabila anda melancong ke negara di mana anda tidak bercakap bahasa "
"tempatan dengan yakin.\n"
"\n"
"## Apa yang Anda Mungkin Perlukan Semasa Daftar Masuk\n"
"\n"
"Penyambut tetamu mungkin akan meminta anda:\n"
"\n"
"- Nama penuh anda\n"
"- Pasport atau dokumen pengenalan diri\n"
"- Pengesahan tempahan anda\n"
"- Kad pembayaran\n"
"- Bilangan tetamu\n"
"- Tarikh jangkaan pemergian anda\n"
"\n"
"Anda boleh memulakan perbualan dengan:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Hello, saya ada tempahan.\"\n"
"- \"Hi, saya ingin mendaftar masuk.\"\n"
"- \"Tempahan sepatutnya atas nama Alex Dmowski.\"\n"
"- \"Saya tempah bilik melalui laman web tempahan.\"\n"
"- \"Ini adalah pengesahan tempahan saya.\"\n"
"\n"
"Jika penyambut tetamu tidak dapat mencari tempahan anda, bertenang dan "
"berikan lebih banyak maklumat:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Boleh anda periksa nombor tempahan?\"\n"
"- \"Saya menerima emel pengesahan semalam.\"\n"
"- \"Tempahan mungkin atas nama pasangan saya.\"\n"
"- \"Adakah membantu jika saya tunjukkan pengesahan?\"\n"
"\n"
"## Sahkan Butiran Penting\n"
"\n"
"Sebelum menerima bilik, sahkan bahawa butiran tempahan adalah betul.\n"
"\n"
"Anda mungkin ingin semak:\n"
"\n"
"- Jenis bilik\n"
"- Bilangan malam\n"
"- Jumlah harga\n"
"- Sama ada sarapan termasuk\n"
"- Bilangan dan saiz katil\n"
"- Masa keluar\n"
"- Sebarang yuran atau deposit tambahan\n"
"\n"
"Soalan berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Boleh anda sahkan jenis bilik yang saya tempah?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah sarapan termasuk dalam harga?\"\n"
"- \"Pukul berapa masa keluar?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah terdapat deposit keselamatan?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah sebarang caj tambahan?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah bilik telah dibayar?\"\n"
"- \"Boleh saya dapatkan resit, sila?\"\n"
"\n"
"Jangan takut untuk meminta penyambut tetamu mengulangi maklumat:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Maaf, boleh anda ulangi?\"\n"
"- \"Boleh anda bercakap lebih perlahan, sila?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda kata masa keluar pukul sebelas?\"\n"
"- \"Boleh anda tuliskan untuk saya?\"\n"
"\n"
"## Tanya Mengenai Perkhidmatan Hotel\n"
"\n"
"Daftar masuk adalah masa yang baik untuk bertanya soalan praktikal mengenai "
"penginapan anda.\n"
"\n"
"### Wi-Fi\n"
"\n"
"- \"Adakah Wi-Fi termasuk?\"\n"
"- \"Apakah kata laluan Wi-Fi?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah Wi-Fi berfungsi di dalam bilik?\"\n"
"\n"
"### Sarapan\n"
"\n"
"- \"Pukul berapa sarapan dihidangkan?\"\n"
"- \"Di mana kawasan sarapan?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda mempunyai pilihan vegetarian?\"\n"
"- \"Bolehkah saya tambah sarapan ke tempahan saya?\"\n"
"\n"
"### Kemudahan hotel\n"
"\n"
"- \"Adakah hotel mempunyai gim?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah tempat untuk menyimpan bagasi saya?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda mempunyai perkhidmatan dobi?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah perkhidmatan bilik tersedia?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah terdapat restoran di hotel?\"\n"
"\n"
"### Pengangkutan dan maklumat tempatan\n"
"\n"
"- \"Boleh anda membantu panggil teksi?\"\n"
"- \"Apakah cara paling mudah untuk sampai ke pusat bandar?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah terdapat perhentian bas berdekatan?\"\n"
"- \"Boleh anda cadangkan restoran di kawasan ini?\"\n"
"\n"
"## Buat Permintaan Khusus\n"
"\n"
"Adalah lebih baik untuk membuat permintaan penting sebelum tiba, tetapi "
"anda juga boleh bertanya di kaunter penerimaan tetamu.\n"
"\n"
"Permintaan biasa termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- Bilik yang tenang\n"
"- Bilik di tingkat lebih tinggi atau lebih rendah\n"
"- Dua katil berasingan\n"
"- Katil yang lebih besar\n"
"- Katil bayi\n"
"- Bilik mudah diakses\n"
"- Tuala atau bantal tambahan\n"
"- Daftar masuk awal\n"
"- Keluar lewat\n"
"- Bilik jauh dari lif\n"
"\n"
"Frasa berguna:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Bolehkah dapatkan bilik yang tenang?\"\n"
"- \"Boleh saya dapatkan bilik jauh dari lif?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda mempunyai bilik di tingkat lebih tinggi?\"\n"
"- \"Boleh kami dapatkan dua katil berasingan?\"\n"
"- \"Bolehkah daftar keluar lebih lewat?\"\n"
"- \"Boleh anda hantar tuala tambahan ke bilik?\"\n"
"\n"
"Menggunakan \"Bolehkah saya…?\", \"Adakah mungkin…?\" dan \"Adakah anda "
"mempunyai…?\" menjadikan permintaan anda kedengaran sopan dan alami.\n"
"\n"
"## Tangani Masalah Biasa\n"
"\n"
"Kadang-kadang bilik belum siap, butiran tempahan tidak betul, atau bilik "
"tidak padan dengan apa yang anda tempah.\n"
"\n"
"### Bilik tidak siap\n"
"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda tahu bila bilik akan siap?\"\n"
"- \"Bolehkah saya tinggalkan bagasi saya di sini?\"\n"
"- \"Boleh beritahu saya bila saya boleh mendaftar masuk?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah tempat untuk saya tunggu?\"\n"
"\n"
"### Tempahan tidak dapat ditemui\n"
"\n"
"- \"Saya ada emel pengesahan. Boleh anda periksa?\"\n"
"- \"Boleh cari menggunakan rujukan tempahan?\"\n"
"- \"Tempahan mungkin di bawah nama lain.\"\n"
"- \"Boley anda hubungi platform tempahan?\"\n"
"\n"
"### Bilik berbeza dari tempahan\n"
"\n"
"- \"Saya percaya saya tempah bilik double.\"\n"
"- \"Pengesahan saya mengatakan sarapan termasuk.\"\n"
"- \"Saya minta dua katil berasingan.\"\n"
"- \"Boleh anda periksa tempahan asal?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah bilik lain tersedia?\"\n"
"\n"
"### Terdapat masalah dengan bilik\n"
"\n"
"- \"Penyejuk udara tidak berfungsi.\"\n"
"- \"Bilik belum dibersihkan.\"\n"
"- \"Terdapat banyak bunyi dari bilik sebelah.\"\n"
"- \"Wi-Fi tidak berfungsi di bilik saya.\"\n"
"- \"Boleh seseorang periksa?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah mungkin untuk tukar bilik?\"\n"
"\n"
"Terangkan masalah dengan jelas, jelaskan apa yang anda harapkan, dan minta "
"penyelesaian tertentu.\n"
"\n"
"## Fahami Soalan Lazim Penyambut Tetamu\n"
"\n"
"Penyambut tetamu mungkin bertanya:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Bolehkah saya tahu nama anda?\"\n"
"- \"Boleh saya lihat pasport atau ID?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda mempunyai pengesahan tempahan?\"\n"
"- \"Berapa malam anda akan tinggal?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda akan bayar dengan kad atau tunai?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda ingin termasuk sarapan?\"\n"
"- \"Perlukah pertolongan dengan bagasi anda?\"\n"
"- \"Mahukah panggilan kejut?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda mempunyai permintaan khas?\"\n"
"\n"
"Anda tidak perlu memberi jawapan panjang. Respons yang jelas dan langsung "
"biasanya yang terbaik.\n"
"\n"
"Sebagai contoh:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Ya, tempahan di bawah Dmowski. Saya akan tinggal selama tiga malam, dan "
"saya akan bayar dengan kad.\"\n"
"\n"
"## Perbualan Daftar Masuk Yang Mudah\n"
"\n"
"Perbualan biasa mungkin mengikuti struktur ini:\n"
"\n"
"1. Sapa penyambut tetamu.\n"
"2. Katakan anda ada tempahan.\n"
"3. Berikan nama dan pengenalan anda.\n"
"4. Sahkan butiran tempahan anda.\n"
"5. Tanya tentang sarapan, Wi-Fi, atau masa keluar.\n"
"6. Buat mana-mana permintaan khas.\n"
"7. Kumpulkan kunci bilik anda dan arahan.\n"
"8. Ucapkan terima kasih kepada penyambut tetamu.\n"
"\n"
"Contoh:\n"
"\n"
"> **Tetamu:** Hello, saya ada tempahan atas nama Dmowski.  \n"
"> **Penyambut Tetamu:** Sudah tentu. Bolehkah saya lihat pasport anda, "
"sila?  \n"
"> **Tetamu:** Sudah tentu. Ini dia. Adakah sarapan termasuk dalam tempahan "
"saya?  \n"
"> **Penyambut Tetamu:** Ya, ia dihidangkan dari tujuh hingga sepuluh.  \n"
"> **Tetamu:** Baiklah. Boleh juga beritahu saya kata laluan Wi-Fi?  \n"
"> **Penyambut Tetamu:** Ia ditulis pada kad kunci anda.  \n"
"> **Tetamu:** Terima kasih. Pukul berapa masa keluar?  \n"
"> **Penyambut Tetamu:** Masa keluar pada pukul sebelas.  \n"
"> **Tetamu:** Sesuai. Terima kasih atas bantuan anda.\n"
"\n"
"## Senario Latihan\n"
"\n"
"Dalam lakonan ini, anda tiba di hotel di mana anda sudah mempunyai "
"tempahan. Penyambut tetamu AI akan meminta butiran anda, menerangkan "
"perkhidmatan hotel, dan menjawab soalan anda.\n"
"\n"
"Semasa perbualan, cuba untuk:\n"
"\n"
"- Perkenalkan diri anda dan sahkan tempahan anda.\n"
"- Tanya sekurang-kurangnya dua soalan mengenai hotel.\n"
"- Buat satu permintaan yang sopan.\n"
"- Sahkan butiran penting dengan mengulanginya.\n"
"- Tanggapi masalah yang tidak dijangka jika timbul.\n"
"\n"
"Fokus untuk berkomunikasi dengan jelas daripada menggunakan tatabahasa yang "
"sempurna. Daftar masuk yang berjaya adalah apabila anda dan penyambut "
"tetamu memahami apa yang perlu dilakukan seterusnya."

