#: src/features/RolePlay/scenarios/in-the-restaurant.ts:58
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid ""
"Eating at a restaurant involves several short conversations: asking for a "
"table, understanding the menu, ordering food, making requests, handling "
"problems, and paying the bill.\n"
"\n"
"You do not need complicated sentences. Clear questions, polite requests, "
"and confirming important details will help you communicate successfully.\n"
"\n"
"## Arriving at the Restaurant\n"
"\n"
"When you enter, a member of staff may ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Do you have a reservation?”\n"
"- “What name is the reservation under?”\n"
"- “How many people are in your party?”\n"
"- “Would you prefer to sit inside or outside?”\n"
"- “Would you like a table by the window?”\n"
"- “Is this table all right?”\n"
"\n"
"If you have a reservation, you can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “Hello, I have a reservation.”\n"
"- “The reservation is under Dmowski.”\n"
"- “I booked a table for two at seven.”\n"
"- “We should have a reservation for four people.”\n"
"- “One more person will be joining us shortly.”\n"
"\n"
"If you do not have a reservation, say:\n"
"\n"
"- “Do you have a table for two?”\n"
"- “We don’t have a reservation. Is there anything available?”\n"
"- “How long is the wait for a table?”\n"
"- “Could we sit outside?”\n"
"- “Would it be possible to sit somewhere quiet?”\n"
"\n"
"You may hear:\n"
"\n"
"- “Your table will be ready in about fifteen minutes.”\n"
"- “We only have tables outside at the moment.”\n"
"- “We can seat you at the bar.”\n"
"- “Unfortunately, we are fully booked.”\n"
"- “Please follow me.”\n"
"\n"
"## Asking for the Menu\n"
"\n"
"After you sit down, the waiter may give you a menu and ask about drinks.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could we see the menu, please?”\n"
"- “Do you have a menu in English?”\n"
"- “Could I have the drinks menu?”\n"
"- “Do you have a children’s menu?”\n"
"- “Is there a separate dessert menu?”\n"
"- “Could we have a few more minutes?”\n"
"\n"
"If you are not ready to order, say:\n"
"\n"
"- “We’re still deciding.”\n"
"- “Could you give us another minute?”\n"
"- “I’m ready to order drinks, but not food yet.”\n"
"- “Could you come back in five minutes?”\n"
"\n"
"You do not need to rush. It is normal to ask for more time.\n"
"\n"
"## Ordering Drinks\n"
"\n"
"The waiter may ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Can I get you something to drink?”\n"
"- “Would you like still or sparkling water?”\n"
"- “Can I bring you anything from the bar?”\n"
"- “Would you like to see the wine list?”\n"
"\n"
"You can order by saying:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could I have a glass of water, please?”\n"
"- “I’d like a sparkling water.”\n"
"- “Could we have a bottle of still water for the table?”\n"
"- “I’ll have an orange juice.”\n"
"- “Could I get a coffee after the meal?”\n"
"- “What non-alcoholic drinks do you have?”\n"
"- “Do you have any alcohol-free beer?”\n"
"\n"
"Useful water vocabulary:\n"
"\n"
"- **Still water** — water without bubbles\n"
"- **Sparkling water** — carbonated water\n"
"- **Tap water** — water from the public water supply\n"
"- **Bottled water** — water served from a bottle\n"
"\n"
"You can ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Is tap water available?”\n"
"- “Is the water complimentary?”\n"
"- “Could we have some ice?”\n"
"- “Could I have that without ice?”\n"
"\n"
"## Understanding the Menu\n"
"\n"
"Menus often contain unfamiliar ingredients or cooking methods. It is "
"completely normal to ask questions.\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “What is this dish?”\n"
"- “What does this come with?”\n"
"- “How is it prepared?”\n"
"- “What kind of meat is used?”\n"
"- “Is this dish spicy?”\n"
"- “Is it very rich?”\n"
"- “Is this served hot or cold?”\n"
"- “What is the sauce made from?”\n"
"- “Does this come with a side dish?”\n"
"- “Is this enough for one person?”\n"
"- “Could you explain the difference between these two dishes?”\n"
"\n"
"Common menu sections include:\n"
"\n"
"- **Starter or appetizer** — a small dish served before the main course\n"
"- **Main course or entrée** — the central dish of the meal\n"
"- **Side dish** — a smaller dish served with the main course\n"
"- **Dessert** — a sweet dish served at the end\n"
"- **Special** — a dish that may only be available that day\n"
"- **Set menu** — several courses offered together for a fixed price\n"
"\n"
"## Ask for a Recommendation\n"
"\n"
"When you are unsure what to order, ask the waiter for help.\n"
"\n"
"You can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “What would you recommend?”\n"
"- “What is your most popular dish?”\n"
"- “What is today’s special?”\n"
"- “Which dish is not too spicy?”\n"
"- “What would you recommend for someone who likes fish?”\n"
"- “I’d like something light. What would you suggest?”\n"
"- “Which vegetarian dish would you recommend?”\n"
"- “What is the difference between these two options?”\n"
"\n"
"It helps to explain your preferences:\n"
"\n"
"- “I like spicy food.”\n"
"- “I’d prefer something light.”\n"
"- “I don’t eat red meat.”\n"
"- “I’m looking for something filling.”\n"
"- “I’d like to try something local.”\n"
"- “I don’t like very sweet sauces.”\n"
"\n"
"A good recommendation should match what you enjoy, not simply what is "
"popular.\n"
"\n"
"## Place Your Order\n"
"\n"
"Common ways to order include:\n"
"\n"
"- “I’d like the tomato soup to start.”\n"
"- “I’ll have the grilled salmon.”\n"
"- “Could I get the chicken salad?”\n"
"- “For my main course, I’d like the pasta.”\n"
"- “I think I’ll try the daily special.”\n"
"- “We’d like to share the starter.”\n"
"- “Could we order one more side dish?”\n"
"\n"
"A typical order might sound like this:\n"
"\n"
"> “I’d like the mushroom soup as a starter and the grilled chicken for my "
"main course. Could I have the salad instead of the fries?”\n"
"\n"
"The waiter may ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Are you ready to order?”\n"
"- “What would you like to start with?”\n"
"- “And for your main course?”\n"
"- “Would you like any side dishes?”\n"
"- “How would you like your steak cooked?”\n"
"- “Would you like anything else?”\n"
"\n"
"## Ask for Changes to a Dish\n"
"\n"
"Restaurants can often make small changes, although not every request will "
"be possible.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could I have this without onions?”\n"
"- “Could you leave out the cheese?”\n"
"- “Could I have the sauce on the side?”\n"
"- “Can I replace the fries with a salad?”\n"
"- “Could I add some grilled vegetables?”\n"
"- “Could you make it less spicy?”\n"
"- “Could I have the dressing separately?”\n"
"- “Is it possible to order a smaller portion?”\n"
"- “Could we share this dish?”\n"
"\n"
"The waiter may respond:\n"
"\n"
"- “Certainly.”\n"
"- “That should be possible.”\n"
"- “There is an additional charge.”\n"
"- “Unfortunately, the sauce is prepared in advance.”\n"
"- “You can choose a different side.”\n"
"- “Let me check with the kitchen.”\n"
"\n"
"## Explain Allergies and Dietary Requirements\n"
"\n"
"Tell the waiter clearly if you have an allergy or an important dietary "
"restriction.\n"
"\n"
"You can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “I’m allergic to peanuts.”\n"
"- “I have a severe nut allergy.”\n"
"- “I cannot eat gluten.”\n"
"- “I’m lactose intolerant.”\n"
"- “I don’t eat meat.”\n"
"- “I’m vegan.”\n"
"- “I need a dairy-free option.”\n"
"- “Does this contain shellfish?”\n"
"- “Is this suitable for vegetarians?”\n"
"- “Could you check with the kitchen?”\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Is this prepared near any nuts?”\n"
"- “Does the sauce contain dairy?”\n"
"- “Is the soup made with chicken stock?”\n"
"- “Does this contain raw egg?”\n"
"- “Is there a gluten-free version?”\n"
"- “Can this dish be prepared without cheese?”\n"
"\n"
"For a serious allergy, do not rely only on symbols printed on the menu. "
"Explain the allergy directly and ask the waiter to confirm with the "
"kitchen.\n"
"\n"
"## Choose How Meat Is Cooked\n"
"\n"
"When ordering steak or some other meats, the waiter may ask:\n"
"\n"
"> “How would you like that cooked?”\n"
"\n"
"Common options include:\n"
"\n"
"- **Rare** — cooked briefly and red inside\n"
"- **Medium rare** — warm and red in the centre\n"
"- **Medium** — pink in the centre\n"
"- **Medium well** — only slightly pink\n"
"- **Well done** — fully cooked through\n"
"\n"
"You can answer:\n"
"\n"
"- “Medium, please.”\n"
"- “I’d like it well done.”\n"
"- “Could you cook it medium rare?”\n"
"- “Please make sure it is fully cooked.”\n"
"\n"
"## Confirm Your Order\n"
"\n"
"Before leaving the table, the waiter may repeat the order.\n"
"\n"
"Listen carefully and correct any mistakes:\n"
"\n"
"- “Yes, that’s correct.”\n"
"- “Actually, I ordered the salmon, not the chicken.”\n"
"- “The salad should be without onions.”\n"
"- “We ordered two soups, not one.”\n"
"- “Could you repeat the side dishes?”\n"
"- “Does that include the extra vegetables?”\n"
"- “Yes, but please put the sauce on the side.”\n"
"\n"
"Repeating important details helps prevent misunderstandings.\n"
"\n"
"## Ask for Something During the Meal\n"
"\n"
"You may need an extra item after the food arrives.\n"
"\n"
"Useful requests include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could we have some more water?”\n"
"- “Could I get another fork?”\n"
"- “Could we have some extra napkins?”\n"
"- “Could I have some salt and pepper?”\n"
"- “Could you bring us another plate?”\n"
"- “Could I have some ketchup?”\n"
"- “Could we get another basket of bread?”\n"
"- “Could you warm this up, please?”\n"
"- “Could I order another drink?”\n"
"\n"
"To get the waiter’s attention politely, say:\n"
"\n"
"- “Excuse me.”\n"
"- “Sorry, could you help us?”\n"
"- “When you have a moment, could we have some more water?”\n"
"\n"
"Avoid shouting or snapping your fingers.\n"
"\n"
"## Respond When the Waiter Checks on You\n"
"\n"
"The waiter may ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “How is everything?”\n"
"- “Is your food all right?”\n"
"- “Can I get you anything else?”\n"
"- “Are you enjoying your meal?”\n"
"\n"
"If everything is good, say:\n"
"\n"
"- “Everything is great, thank you.”\n"
"- “The food is delicious.”\n"
"- “Yes, everything is fine.”\n"
"- “We’re enjoying it, thank you.”\n"
"\n"
"If something is wrong, this is a good opportunity to explain it.\n"
"\n"
"## Handle an Incorrect Order\n"
"\n"
"Mistakes can happen. Explain the problem calmly and clearly.\n"
"\n"
"You can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “Excuse me, I think this is the wrong dish.”\n"
"- “I ordered the salmon, but this is chicken.”\n"
"- “I asked for this without cheese.”\n"
"- “This isn’t what I ordered.”\n"
"- “We’re still waiting for one dish.”\n"
"- “I think this belongs to another table.”\n"
"- “Could you check our order, please?”\n"
"\n"
"Ask for a clear solution:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could you replace it, please?”\n"
"- “Could you bring the dish I ordered?”\n"
"- “Could you remove this from the bill?”\n"
"- “Could you check how long the correct dish will take?”\n"
"- “Would it be possible to keep the other meals warm?”\n"
"\n"
"## Complain About the Food Politely\n"
"\n"
"If the food is not properly prepared, describe the specific problem.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “The food is cold.”\n"
"- “The steak is overcooked.”\n"
"- “This is much spicier than I expected.”\n"
"- “The chicken does not seem fully cooked.”\n"
"- “The soup is too salty.”\n"
"- “There is an ingredient I asked to have removed.”\n"
"- “This dish tastes unusual.”\n"
"- “Could you ask the kitchen to check it?”\n"
"\n"
"A polite but clear complaint might be:\n"
"\n"
"> “Excuse me, I ordered the steak medium, but it is well done. Would it be "
"possible to replace it?”\n"
"\n"
"You do not need to apologize for reporting a genuine problem.\n"
"\n"
"## Ask About a Delayed Order\n"
"\n"
"If you have been waiting a long time, ask for an update:\n"
"\n"
"- “Excuse me, could you check on our order?”\n"
"- “Do you know how much longer it will take?”\n"
"- “We’ve been waiting for about forty minutes.”\n"
"- “Is there a delay in the kitchen?”\n"
"- “One person at our table still hasn’t received their food.”\n"
"- “Could all the meals be served together?”\n"
"- “We need to leave soon. Is the order almost ready?”\n"
"\n"
"Stay factual and explain what you need.\n"
"\n"
"## Order Dessert or Coffee\n"
"\n"
"After the main course, the waiter may ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Would you like to see the dessert menu?”\n"
"- “Can I interest you in dessert?”\n"
"- “Would you like coffee or tea?”\n"
"- “Can I clear these plates?”\n"
"\n"
"You can respond:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could we see the dessert menu?”\n"
"- “What desserts do you recommend?”\n"
"- “We’ll share one dessert.”\n"
"- “I’ll have a coffee, please.”\n"
"- “Could I have a decaffeinated coffee?”\n"
"- “No dessert, thank you.”\n"
"- “Just the bill, please.”\n"
"\n"
"## Ask to Take Leftovers Home\n"
"\n"
"In some countries and restaurants, you can ask to take unfinished food with "
"you.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could I take this home?”\n"
"- “Could you pack this for me?”\n"
"- “Could I have a takeaway box?”\n"
"- “Could you pack the sauce separately?”\n"
"- “Is it safe to reheat this tomorrow?”\n"
"\n"
"You may also hear:\n"
"\n"
"- “Would you like me to box that for you?”\n"
"- “Would you like to take the rest with you?”\n"
"\n"
"## Ask for the Bill\n"
"\n"
"At the end of the meal, say:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could we have the bill, please?”\n"
"- “Could I get the check, please?”\n"
"- “We’re ready to pay.”\n"
"- “Could you bring the card machine?”\n"
"- “Can we pay at the table?”\n"
"- “Do we pay here or at the counter?”\n"
"\n"
"**Bill** is more common in British English, while **check** is more common "
"in American English.\n"
"\n"
"## Pay Together or Separately\n"
"\n"
"The waiter may ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Will that be together or separate?”\n"
"- “Would you like to split the bill?”\n"
"- “How would you like to pay?”\n"
"\n"
"Useful responses include:\n"
"\n"
"- “We’ll pay together.”\n"
"- “Could we pay separately?”\n"
"- “Could we split the bill equally?”\n"
"- “I’ll pay for everything.”\n"
"- “Could I pay for these two items?”\n"
"- “Can we use two different cards?”\n"
"- “Could you divide the total between three people?”\n"
"\n"
"If you need to explain exactly what you ordered, say:\n"
"\n"
"> “I had the soup, the salmon, and one sparkling water.”\n"
"\n"
"## Check the Bill\n"
"\n"
"Before paying, check that the items and total are correct.\n"
"\n"
"You can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could you explain this charge?”\n"
"- “I think there is an extra item on the bill.”\n"
"- “We only ordered one bottle of water.”\n"
"- “Was the service charge included?”\n"
"- “Is the tip already included?”\n"
"- “Could you remove this item? It was sent back.”\n"
"- “Could I have an itemized bill?”\n"
"- “Could I have a receipt?”\n"
"\n"
"An **itemized bill** lists each food and drink item separately.\n"
"\n"
"## Pay and Leave a Tip\n"
"\n"
"Useful payment phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “I’ll pay by card.”\n"
"- “Can I pay in cash?”\n"
"- “Do you accept contactless payments?”\n"
"- “Could I pay in a different currency?”\n"
"- “Could I have a receipt?”\n"
"- “Can I add a tip by card?”\n"
"- “Is service included?”\n"
"- “Please keep the change.”\n"
"\n"
"Tipping customs vary by country. Check whether a service charge has already "
"been added before leaving an additional tip.\n"
"\n"
"## A Simple Restaurant Conversation\n"
"\n"
"A typical conversation may look like this:\n"
"\n"
"> **Waiter:** Good evening. Do you have a reservation?  \n"
"> **Customer:** Yes, I booked a table for two under Dmowski.  \n"
"> **Waiter:** Certainly. Please follow me. Can I bring you something to "
"drink?  \n"
"> **Customer:** Could we have a bottle of still water, please?  \n"
"> **Waiter:** Of course. Are you ready to order?  \n"
"> **Customer:** I need another minute. What would you recommend for someone "
"who likes fish?  \n"
"> **Waiter:** The grilled salmon is very popular. It comes with potatoes "
"and vegetables.  \n"
"> **Customer:** Does the sauce contain dairy?  \n"
"> **Waiter:** Yes, but we can serve it without the sauce.  \n"
"> **Customer:** Great. I’ll have the salmon without the sauce. Could I "
"replace the potatoes with a salad?  \n"
"> **Waiter:** Certainly.  \n"
"> **Customer:** Thank you.\n"
"\n"
"## A Simple Restaurant Formula\n"
"\n"
"Use this structure during a restaurant visit:\n"
"\n"
"1. **Arrive:** Confirm your reservation or ask for a table.\n"
"2. **Ask:** Request the menu and ask about unfamiliar dishes.\n"
"3. **Choose:** Order food and drinks clearly.\n"
"4. **Clarify:** Explain allergies, preferences, and requested changes.\n"
"5. **Confirm:** Listen while the waiter repeats the order.\n"
"6. **Respond:** Ask for anything else you need during the meal.\n"
"7. **Resolve:** Explain any problems and request a solution.\n"
"8. **Pay:** Ask for the bill, check it, and choose a payment method.\n"
"\n"
"For example:\n"
"\n"
"> “I’d like the grilled chicken, but could I have it without onions and "
"with a salad instead of fries?”\n"
"\n"
"## Practice Scenario\n"
"\n"
"In this roleplay, you are dining at the Riverside Kitchen. The AI waiter "
"will welcome you, help you understand the menu, take your order, and "
"respond to your requests.\n"
"\n"
"During the conversation, try to:\n"
"\n"
"- Ask for a table or confirm a reservation.\n"
"- Order a drink and a main course.\n"
"- Ask at least one question about a menu item.\n"
"- Request a recommendation.\n"
"- Mention a dietary preference or ask for a change.\n"
"- Confirm an important detail about your order.\n"
"- Respond to one small problem with the meal or service.\n"
"- Ask for the bill and explain how you would like to pay.\n"
"\n"
"Focus on communicating clearly and politely. Perfect grammar is less "
"important than making sure the waiter understands your order and your needs."
msgstr ""
"Makan di restoran melibatkan beberapa perbualan pendek: meminta meja, "
"memahami menu, memesan makanan, membuat permintaan, menangani masalah, dan "
"membayar bil.\n"
"\n"
"Anda tidak memerlukan ayat yang rumit. Soalan yang jelas, permintaan yang "
"sopan, dan pengesahan butiran penting akan membantu anda berkomunikasi "
"dengan berjaya.\n"
"\n"
"## Tiba di Restoran\n"
"\n"
"Apabila anda masuk, seorang ahli kakitangan mungkin bertanya:\n"
"\n"
"- “Adakah anda mempunyai tempahan?”\n"
"- “Atas nama siapa tempahan itu?”\n"
"- “Berapa ramai orang dalam kumpulan anda?”\n"
"- “Adakah anda lebih suka duduk di dalam atau di luar?”\n"
"- “Adakah anda mahu meja di tepi tingkap?”\n"
"- “Adakah meja ini sesuai?”\n"
"\n"
"Jika anda mempunyai tempahan, anda boleh berkata:\n"
"\n"
"- “Hello, saya ada tempahan.”\n"
"- “Tempahan atas nama Dmowski.”\n"
"- “Saya tempah meja untuk dua pada pukul tujuh.”\n"
"- “Kami sepatutnya ada tempahan untuk empat orang.”\n"
"- “Seorang lagi akan menyertai kami sebentar lagi.”\n"
"\n"
"Jika anda tidak mempunyai tempahan, katakan:\n"
"\n"
"- “Adakah anda mempunyai meja untuk dua?”\n"
"- “Kami tidak mempunyai tempahan. Adakah ada yang tersedia?”\n"
"- “Berapa lamakah menunggu untuk meja?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah kami duduk di luar?”\n"
"- “Adakah mungkin untuk duduk di tempat yang tenang?”\n"
"\n"
"Anda mungkin mendengar:\n"
"\n"
"- “Meja anda akan siap dalam masa kira-kira lima belas minit.”\n"
"- “Kami hanya mempunyai meja di luar pada masa ini.”\n"
"- “Kami boleh letakkan anda di bar.”\n"
"- “Malangnya, kami penuh.”\n"
"- “Sila ikut saya.”\n"
"\n"
"## Meminta Menu\n"
"\n"
"Selepas anda duduk, pelayan mungkin memberikan anda menu dan bertanya "
"tentang minuman.\n"
"\n"
"Frasa berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- “Bolehkah kami melihat menu, sila?”\n"
"- “Adakah anda mempunyai menu dalam Bahasa Inggeris?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah saya mendapat menu minuman?”\n"
"- “Adakah anda mempunyai menu kanak-kanak?”\n"
"- “Adakah terdapat menu pencuci mulut yang berasingan?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah kami mendapat beberapa minit lagi?”\n"
"\n"
"Jika anda belum bersedia untuk memesan, katakan:\n"
"\n"
"- “Kami masih membuat keputusan.”\n"
"- “Bolehkah anda berikan kami seminit lagi?”\n"
"- “Saya bersedia untuk memesan minuman, tetapi belum makanan.”\n"
"- “Bolehkah anda kembali dalam lima minit?”\n"
"\n"
"Anda tidak perlu tergesa-gesa. Adalah normal untuk meminta lebih banyak "
"masa.\n"
"\n"
"## Memesan Minuman\n"
"\n"
"Pelayan mungkin bertanya:\n"
"\n"
"- “Bolehkah saya dapatkan anda sesuatu untuk diminum?”\n"
"- “Adakah anda mahu air biasa atau berkarbonat?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah saya bawa apa-apa dari bar?”\n"
"- “Adakah anda mahu melihat senarai wain?”\n"
"\n"
"Anda boleh memesan dengan berkata:\n"
"\n"
"- “Bolehkah saya mendapat segelas air, sila?”\n"
"- “Saya mahu air berkarbonat.”\n"
"- “Bolehkah kami mendapat sebotol air biasa untuk meja?”\n"
"- “Saya akan ambil jus oren.”\n"
"- “Bolehkah saya mendapat kopi selepas makan?”\n"
"- “Apa minuman tanpa alkohol yang anda ada?”\n"
"- “Adakah anda mempunyai bir tanpa alkohol?”\n"
"\n"
"Perkataan berguna tentang air:\n"
"\n"
"- **Air biasa** — air tanpa buih\n"
"- **Air berkarbonat** — air berkarbonat\n"
"- **Air paip** — air dari bekalan air awam\n"
"- **Air botol** — air yang disajikan dari botol\n"
"\n"
"Anda boleh bertanya:\n"
"\n"
"- “Adakah air paip tersedia?”\n"
"- “Adakah air itu percuma?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah kami mendapat sedikit ais?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah saya dapatkannya tanpa ais?”\n"
"\n"
"## Memahami Menu\n"
"\n"
"Menu sering mengandungi bahan atau kaedah memasak yang tidak dikenali. "
"Adalah perkara biasa untuk bertanya soalan.\n"
"\n"
"Soalan berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- “Apakah hidangan ini?”\n"
"- “Apa yang datang bersama ini?”\n"
"- “Bagaimana ia disediakan?”\n"
"- “Apa jenis daging yang digunakan?”\n"
"- “Adakah hidangan ini pedas?”\n"
"- “Adakah ia sangat kaya?”\n"
"- “Adakah ini disajikan panas atau sejuk?”\n"
"- “Apakah sos ini dibuat dari?”\n"
"- “Adakah ini datang dengan hidangan sisi?”\n"
"- “Adakah ini cukup untuk satu orang?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah anda terangkan perbezaan antara dua hidangan ini?”\n"
"\n"
"Bahagian menu yang biasa termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- **Permulaan atau pembuka selera** — hidangan kecil yang disajikan sebelum "
"hidangan utama\n"
"- **Hidangan utama atau entrée** — hidangan utama makan\n"
"- **Hidangan sisi** — hidangan kecil yang disajikan bersama hidangan utama\n"
"- **Pencuci mulut** — hidangan manis yang disajikan di penghujung\n"
"- **Istimewa** — hidangan yang mungkin hanya tersedia pada hari itu\n"
"- **Menu set** — beberapa hidangan yang ditawarkan bersama dengan harga "
"tetap\n"
"\n"
"## Meminta Cadangan\n"
"\n"
"Apabila anda tidak pasti apa yang hendak dipesan, minta bantuan pelayan.\n"
"\n"
"Anda boleh berkata:\n"
"\n"
"- “Apa yang anda cadangkan?”\n"
"- “Apa hidangan anda yang paling popular?”\n"
"- “Apa yang istimewa hari ini?”\n"
"- “Hidangan mana yang tidak terlalu pedas?”\n"
"- “Apa yang anda cadangkan untuk seseorang yang suka ikan?”\n"
"- “Saya mahu sesuatu yang ringan. Apa yang anda cadangkan?”\n"
"- “Hidangan vegetarian mana yang anda cadangkan?”\n"
"- “Apa perbezaan antara dua pilihan ini?”\n"
"\n"
"Ia membantu menjelaskan pilihan anda:\n"
"\n"
"- “Saya suka makanan pedas.”\n"
"- “Saya lebih suka sesuatu yang ringan.”\n"
"- “Saya tidak makan daging merah.”\n"
"- “Saya mencari sesuatu yang mengenyangkan.”\n"
"- “Saya mahu cuba sesuatu yang tempatan.”\n"
"- “Saya tidak suka sos yang sangat manis.”\n"
"\n"
"Cadangan yang baik harus sesuai dengan apa yang anda nikmati, bukan sekadar "
"apa yang popular.\n"
"\n"
"## Membuat Pesanan Anda\n"
"\n"
"Cara biasa untuk memesan termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- “Saya mahu sup tomato untuk memulakan.”\n"
"- “Saya mahu salmon panggang.”\n"
"- “Bolehkah saya dapatkan salad ayam?”\n"
"- “Untuk hidangan utama saya, saya mahu pasta.”\n"
"- “Saya rasa saya akan mencuba istimewa hari ini.”\n"
"- “Kami mahu berkongsi pembuka selera.”\n"
"- “Bolehkah kami memesan satu lagi hidangan sisi?”\n"
"\n"
"Pesanan biasa mungkin berbunyi seperti ini:\n"
"\n"
"> “Saya mahu sup cendawan sebagai permulaan dan ayam panggang untuk "
"hidangan utama saya. Bolehkah saya mendapatkan salad dan bukan kentang "
"goreng?”\n"
"\n"
"Pelayan mungkin bertanya:\n"
"\n"
"- “Adakah anda bersedia untuk memesan?”\n"
"- “Apa yang anda mahu sebagai permulaan?”\n"
"- “Dan untuk hidangan utama anda?”\n"
"- “Adakah anda mahu mana-mana hidangan sisi?”\n"
"- “Bagaimana anda mahu steak anda dimasak?”\n"
"- “Adakah anda mahu apa-apa lagi?”\n"
"\n"
"## Meminta Perubahan kepada Hidangan\n"
"\n"
"Restoran selalunya boleh membuat perubahan kecil, walaupun tidak setiap "
"permintaan akan dapat dipenuhi.\n"
"\n"
"Frasa berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- “Bolehkah saya dapatkan ini tanpa bawang?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah anda tinggalkan keju?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah saya dapatkan sos di sebelah?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah saya menggantikan kentang goreng dengan salad?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah saya menambah sayur-sayuran panggang?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah anda membuatnya kurang pedas?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah saya dapatkan pemakaian secara berasingan?”\n"
"- “Adakah mungkin memesan bahagian yang lebih kecil?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah kami berkongsi hidangan ini?”\n"
"\n"
"Pelayan mungkin menjawab:\n"
"\n"
"- “Sudah tentu.”\n"
"- “Itu sepatutnya boleh dilakukan.”\n"
"- “Ada caj tambahan.”\n"
"- “Malangnya, sos disediakan lebih awal.”\n"
"- “Anda boleh memilih hidangan sisi yang berbeza.”\n"
"- “Biar saya berbincang dengan dapur.”\n"
"\n"
"## Terangkan Alergi dan Keperluan Diet\n"
"\n"
"Beritahu pelayan dengan jelas jika anda mempunyai alergi atau sekatan diet "
"yang penting.\n"
"\n"
"Anda boleh berkata:\n"
"\n"
"- “Saya alah kepada kacang tanah.”\n"
"- “Saya mempunyai alahan kacang yang teruk.”\n"
"- “Saya tidak boleh makan gluten.”\n"
"- “Saya tidak toleran laktosa.”\n"
"- “Saya tidak makan daging.”\n"
"- “Saya vegan.”\n"
"- “Saya perlukan pilihan bebas tenusu.”\n"
"- “Adakah ini mengandungi kerang?”\n"
"- “Adakah ini sesuai untuk vegetarian?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah anda periksa dengan dapur?”\n"
"\n"
"Soalan berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- “Adakah ini disediakan berdekatan dengan mana-mana kacang?”\n"
"- “Adakah sos mengandungi tenusu?”\n"
"- “Adakah sup ini dibuat dengan stok ayam?”\n"
"- “Adakah ini mengandungi telur mentah?”\n"
"- “Adakah terdapat versi bebas gluten?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah hidangan ini disediakan tanpa keju?”\n"
"\n"
"Untuk alergi serius, jangan bergantung hanya pada simbol yang dicetak pada "
"menu. Terangkan alergi secara langsung dan minta pelayan mengesahkan dengan "
"dapur.\n"
"\n"
"## Pilih Cara Daging Dimasak\n"
"\n"
"Apabila memesan steak atau beberapa daging lain, pelayan mungkin bertanya:\n"
"\n"
"> “Bagaimana anda mahu itu dimasak?”\n"
"\n"
"Pilihan umum termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- **Rare** — dimasak sebentar dan merah di dalam\n"
"- **Medium rare** — hangat dan merah di tengah\n"
"- **Medium** — merah jambu di tengah\n"
"- **Medium well** — hanya sedikit merah jambu\n"
"- **Well done** — dimasak sepenuhnya\n"
"\n"
"Anda boleh menjawab:\n"
"\n"
"- “Medium, sila.”\n"
"- “Saya mahu ianya masak sepenuhnya.”\n"
"- “Bolehkah anda memasaknya medium rare?”\n"
"- “Sila pastikan ia dimasak sepenuhnya.”\n"
"\n"
"## Sahkan Pesanan Anda\n"
"\n"
"Sebelum meninggalkan meja, pelayan mungkin mengulangi pesanan.\n"
"\n"
"Dengar dengan teliti dan betulkan mana-mana kesilapan:\n"
"\n"
"- “Ya, itu betul.”\n"
"- “Sebenarnya, saya memesan salmon, bukan ayam.”\n"
"- “Salad sepatutnya tanpa bawang.”\n"
"- “Kami memesan dua sup, bukan satu.”\n"
"- “Bolehkah anda ulangkan hidangan sisi?”\n"
"- “Adakah itu termasuk sayur-sayuran tambahan?”\n"
"- “Ya, tetapi sila letakkan sos di sebelah.”\n"
"\n"
"Mengulangi butiran penting membantu mengelakkan salah faham.\n"
"\n"
"## Meminta Sesuatu Semasa Makan\n"
"\n"
"Anda mungkin memerlukan item tambahan selepas makanan tiba.\n"
"\n"
"Permintaan berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- “Bolehkah kami mendapat lebih banyak air?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah saya dapatkan garpu lain?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah kami mendapat tuala ekstra?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah saya mendapat garam dan lada?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah anda bawa kami sepinggan lain?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah saya mempunyai sedikit sos?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah kami mendapat bakul roti lain?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah anda panaskan ini, sila?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah saya memesan minuman lain?”\n"
"\n"
"Untuk mendapatkan perhatian pelayan dengan sopan, katakan:\n"
"\n"
"- “Maafkan saya.”\n"
"- “Maaf, bolehkah anda membantu kami?”\n"
"- “Apabila anda mempunyai masa, bolehkah kami mendapat lebih banyak air?”\n"
"\n"
"Elakkan menjerit atau memetik jari anda.\n"
"\n"
"## Bertindak Balas Apabila Pelayan Memeriksa Anda\n"
"\n"
"Pelayan mungkin bertanya:\n"
"\n"
"- “Bagaimana semuanya?”\n"
"- “Adakah makanan anda baik-baik saja?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah saya dapatkan apa-apa lagi?”\n"
"- “Adakah anda menikmati hidangan anda?”\n"
"\n"
"Jika semuanya baik, katakan:\n"
"\n"
"- “Semuanya hebat, terima kasih.”\n"
"- “Makanan ini sedap.”\n"
"- “Ya, semuanya baik.”\n"
"- “Kami menikmatinya, terima kasih.”\n"
"\n"
"Jika ada sesuatu yang salah, ini adalah peluang yang baik untuk "
"menjelaskannya.\n"
"\n"
"## Menangani Pesanan yang Salah\n"
"\n"
"Kesilapan boleh berlaku. Terangkan masalah dengan tenang dan jelas.\n"
"\n"
"Anda boleh berkata:\n"
"\n"
"- “Maafkan saya, saya rasa ini hidangan yang salah.”\n"
"- “Saya memesan salmon, tetapi ini ayam.”\n"
"- “Saya meminta ini tanpa keju.”\n"
"- “Ini bukan apa yang saya pesan.”\n"
"- “Kami masih menunggu satu hidangan.”\n"
"- “Saya fikir ini milik meja lain.”\n"
"- “Bolehkah anda periksa pesanan kami, sila?”\n"
"\n"
"Minta penyelesaian yang jelas:\n"
"\n"
"- “Bolehkah anda gantikannya, sila?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah anda bawa hidangan yang saya pesan?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah anda keluarkan ini dari bil?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah anda periksa berapa lama hidangan yang betul akan mengambil "
"masa?”\n"
"- “Adakah mungkin untuk meletakkan hidangan lain kekal hangat?”\n"
"\n"
"## Mengadu Mengenai Makanan dengan Sopan\n"
"\n"
"Jika makanan tidak disediakan dengan betul, nyatakan masalah tertentu.\n"
"\n"
"Frasa berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- “Makanan ini sejuk.”\n"
"- “Steak ini terlalu masak.”\n"
"- “Ini jauh lebih pedas daripada yang saya jangkakan.”\n"
"- “Ayam ini nampaknya tidak sepenuhnya dimasak.”\n"
"- “Sup ini terlalu masin.”\n"
"- “Terdapat bahan yang saya minta untuk dibuang.”\n"
"- “Hidangan ini mempunyai rasa yang luar biasa.”\n"
"- “Bolehkah anda minta dapur untuk memeriksanya?”\n"
"\n"
"Aduan yang sopan tetapi jelas mungkin seperti ini:\n"
"\n"
"> “Maafkan saya, saya memesan steak medium, tetapi ini terlalu masak. "
"Adakah mungkin untuk menggantikannya?”\n"
"\n"
"Anda tidak perlu meminta maaf kerana melaporkan masalah sebenar.\n"
"\n"
"## Bertanya Mengenai Pesanan yang Tertunda\n"
"\n"
"Jika anda telah menunggu lama, minta kemas kini:\n"
"\n"
"- “Maafkan saya, bolehkah anda periksa pesanan kami?”\n"
"- “Adakah anda tahu berapa lama lagi ia akan mengambil masa?”\n"
"- “Kami telah menunggu selama kira-kira empat puluh minit.”\n"
"- “Adakah terdapat kelewatan di dapur?”\n"
"- “Satu orang di meja kami masih belum menerima makanan mereka.”\n"
"- “Bolehkah semua hidangan disajikan bersama?”\n"
"- “Kami perlu meninggalkan sekejap. Adakah pesanan hampir siap?”\n"
"\n"
"Tetap berfakta dan terangkan apa yang anda perlukan.\n"
"\n"
"## Memesan Pencuci Mulut atau Kopi\n"
"\n"
"Selepas hidangan utama, pelayan mungkin bertanya:\n"
"\n"
"- “Adakah anda mahu melihat menu pencuci mulut?”\n"
"- “Adakah saya menarik minat anda untuk pencuci mulut?”\n"
"- “Adakah anda mahu kopi atau teh?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah saya membersihkan pinggan ini?”\n"
"\n"
"Anda boleh bertindak balas:\n"
"\n"
"- “Bolehkah kami melihat menu pencuci mulut?”\n"
"- “Apa pencuci mulut yang anda cadangkan?”\n"
"- “Kami akan berkongsi satu pencuci mulut.”\n"
"- “Saya mahu kopi, sila.”\n"
"- “Bolehkah saya mendapatkan kopi dekaffein?”\n"
"- “Tiada pencuci mulut, terima kasih.”\n"
"- “Hanya bil, sila.”\n"
"\n"
"## Meminta Membawa Pulang Sisa Makanan\n"
"\n"
"Di beberapa negara dan restoran, anda boleh meminta untuk membawa makanan "
"yang belum selesai bersama anda.\n"
"\n"
"Frasa berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- “Bolehkah saya membawa ini pulang?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah anda membungkus ini untuk saya?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah saya mendapat kotak bawaan?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah anda membungkus sos secara berasingan?”\n"
"- “Adakah selamat untuk dipanaskan semula esok?”\n"
"\n"
"Anda mungkin juga mendengar:\n"
"\n"
"- “Adakah anda mahu saya membungkusnya untuk anda?”\n"
"- “Adakah anda mahu membawa selebihnya?”\n"
"\n"
"## Meminta Bil\n"
"\n"
"Pada akhir hidangan, katakan:\n"
"\n"
"- “Bolehkah kami mendapat bil, sila?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah saya mendapatkan cek, sila?”\n"
"- “Kami bersedia untuk membayar.”\n"
"- “Bolehkah anda bawa mesin kad?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah kami membayar di meja?”\n"
"- “Adakah kami membayar di sini atau di kaunter?”\n"
"\n"
"**Bil** adalah lebih biasa dalam Bahasa Inggeris British, sementara **cek** "
"adalah lebih biasa dalam Bahasa Inggeris Amerika.\n"
"\n"
"## Bayar Bersama atau Berasingan\n"
"\n"
"Pelayan mungkin bertanya:\n"
"\n"
"- “Adakah itu bersama atau berasingan?”\n"
"- “Adakah anda mahu membahagikan bil?”\n"
"- “Bagaimana anda mahu membayar?”\n"
"\n"
"Tindak balas berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- “Kami akan membayar bersama.”\n"
"- “Bolehkah kami membayar berasingan?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah kami membahagikan bil sama rata?”\n"
"- “Saya akan membayar untuk semuanya.”\n"
"- “Bolehkah saya membayar untuk dua item ini?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah kami menggunakan dua kad berbeza?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah anda bahagikan jumlah antara tiga orang?”\n"
"\n"
"Jika anda perlu menjelaskan apa yang anda pesan, katakan:\n"
"\n"
"> “Saya ada sup, salmon, dan satu air berkilau.”\n"
"\n"
"## Periksa Bil\n"
"\n"
"Sebelum membayar, periksa bahawa item dan jumlahnya betul.\n"
"\n"
"Anda boleh berkata:\n"
"\n"
"- “Bolehkah anda terangkan caj ini?”\n"
"- “Saya rasa ada item tambahan dalam bil ini.”\n"
"- “Kami hanya memesan satu botol air.”\n"
"- “Adakah caj perkhidmatan termasuk?”\n"
"- “Adakah tip sudah termasuk?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah anda keluarkan item ini? Ia telah dipulangkan.”\n"
"- “Bolehkah saya mendapatkan bil itemized?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah saya mendapatkan resit?”\n"
"\n"
"Bil **itemized** menyenaraikan setiap item makanan dan minuman secara "
"berasingan.\n"
"\n"
"## Bayar dan Berikan Tip\n"
"\n"
"Frasa pembayaran berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- “Saya akan membayar dengan kad.”\n"
"- “Bolehkah saya membayar tunai?”\n"
"- “Adakah anda menerima pembayaran tanpa sentuh?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah saya membayar dalam mata wang yang berbeza?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah saya mendapatkan resit?”\n"
"- “Bolehkah saya menambah tip dengan kad?”\n"
"- “Adakah perkhidmatan termasuk?”\n"
"- “Sila simpan bakinya.”\n"
"\n"
"Adat memberikan tip berbeza mengikut negara. Periksa sama ada caj "
"perkhidmatan sudah ditambah sebelum meninggalkan tip tambahan.\n"
"\n"
"## Perbualan Restoran Sederhana\n"
"\n"
"Perbualan biasa mungkin seperti ini:\n"
"\n"
"> **Pelayan:** Selamat malam. Adakah anda mempunyai tempahan?  \n"
"> **Pelanggan:** Ya, saya tempah meja untuk dua orang atas nama Dmowski.  \n"
"> **Pelayan:** Sudah tentu. Sila ikut saya. Bolehkah saya bawa anda sesuatu "
"untuk diminum?  \n"
"> **Pelanggan:** Bolehkah kami mendapat sebotol air biasa, sila?  \n"
"> **Pelayan:** Tentu. Adakah anda bersedia untuk memesan?  \n"
"> **Pelanggan:** Saya perlukan satu minit lagi. Apa yang anda cadangkan "
"untuk seseorang yang suka ikan?  \n"
"> **Pelayan:** Salmon panggang sangat popular. Ia datang dengan kentang dan "
"sayur-sayuran.  \n"
"> **Pelanggan:** Adakah sosnya mengandungi tenusu?  \n"
"> **Pelayan:** Ya, tetapi kami boleh menyajikannya tanpa sos.  \n"
"> **Pelanggan:** Hebat. Saya mahu salmon tanpa sos. Bolehkah saya "
"menggantikan kentang dengan salad?  \n"
"> **Pelayan:** Sudah tentu.  \n"
"> **Pelanggan:** Terima kasih.\n"
"\n"
"## Formula Restoran Sederhana\n"
"\n"
"Gunakan struktur ini semasa lawatan restoran:\n"
"\n"
"1. **Tiba:** Sahkan tempahan anda atau minta meja.\n"
"2. **Tanya:** Minta menu dan tanya mengenai hidangan yang tidak dikenali.\n"
"3. **Pilih:** Pesan makanan dan minuman dengan jelas.\n"
"4. **Jelaskan:** Terangkan alergi, keutamaan, dan permintaan perubahan.\n"
"5. **Sahkan:** Dengar semasa pelayan mengulangi pesanan.\n"
"6. **Tindak Balas:** Minta apa sahaja yang anda perlukan semasa makan.\n"
"7. **Selesaikan:** Terangkan sebarang masalah dan minta penyelesaian.\n"
"8. **Bayar:** Minta bil, semak, dan pilih kaedah pembayaran.\n"
"\n"
"Sebagai contoh:\n"
"\n"
"> “Saya mahu ayam panggang, tetapi bolehkah saya mendapatkannya tanpa "
"bawang dan dengan salad dan bukan kentang goreng?”\n"
"\n"
"## Senario Latihan\n"
"\n"
"Dalam permainan peranan ini, anda sedang makan di Riverside Kitchen. "
"Pelayan AI akan menyambut anda, membantu anda memahami menu, mengambil "
"pesanan anda, dan menjawab permintaan anda.\n"
"\n"
"Semasa perbualan, cuba untuk:\n"
"\n"
"- Minta meja atau sahkan tempahan.\n"
"- Pesan minuman dan hidangan utama.\n"
"- Tanya sekurang-kurangnya satu soalan tentang item menu.\n"
"- Minta cadangan.\n"
"- Sebutkan keutamaan pemakanan atau minta perubahan.\n"
"- Sahkan butiran penting mengenai pesanan anda.\n"
"- Bertindak balas terhadap satu masalah kecil dengan hidangan atau "
"perkhidmatan.\n"
"- Minta bil dan jelaskan cara anda ingin membayar.\n"
"\n"
"Fokus pada komunikasi yang jelas dan sopan. Tatabahasa yang sempurna kurang "
"penting daripada memastikan pelayan memahami pesanan anda dan keperluan "
"anda."

