#: src/features/Blog/blogData.tsx:133
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid ""
"I am not a talented software developer. I'm not the fastest one — and "
"definitely not the best. But when the company where I work struggles with "
"something important and urgent, they ask for my help and pay me a lot. No "
"clue why.\n"
"\n"
"The company makes chatbots for entertainment. You know those ads like "
"*“Let’s talk with Albert Einstein”* or *“Let’s chat with Marilyn Monroe.”* "
"Which I find quite stupid — but it works. Well, it had been working, to be "
"precise. The company got stuck. No ideas for new features, no interesting "
"characters. Whoever wanted to try it already had. Revenue slowly declined. "
"The team’s writer, who was hired to craft such personas, couldn’t keep up, "
"and quality was slipping.\n"
"\n"
"Our task was to improve it — with no real idea how. That’s all you need to "
"know about my employer’s management and processes, or lack of processes, "
"vision, plan, responsibilities. But okay.\n"
"\n"
"![img.png](/blog/dog/monroe.webp)\n"
"\n"
"The writer's idea was to create a famous person who had tried another life "
"— so the user could talk, for example, with Donald Trump, who in the middle "
"of his life decided to switch careers and become a painter. Maybe our "
"writer got inspired by Donald’s recently announced drawing, allegedly sent "
"to Epstein. But anyway. The writer gave me a one-page draft about Donald's "
"life after his career pivot.\n"
"\n"
"Which was not enough to create a good AI persona. I needed at least 20 "
"pages of text to fill our QDrant vector store, so the AI RAG system could "
"freely pick well-embedded documents for a proper fine-tuning process. "
"*Sorry for the engineering terms.*\n"
"\n"
"After one day of waiting, I decided to use AI to generate what our writer "
"might have written. It was an act of procrastination. I just wanted to fill "
"the waiting time. Surprisingly, the results were almost identical to what "
"the writer gave me. That, to be honest, astonished me.\n"
"\n"
"It might have been a coincidence, so I wanted to re-check it with real data "
"— with my personal data. Later, I realized that was the wrong decision.\n"
"\n"
"The company was in a rush. *“We needed this persona done yesterday,”* said "
"the founder. I was skeptical that this persona would rejuvenate the "
"company. I asked for two extra days to finish my work. Most of the time I "
"planned to allocate to my experiments.\n"
"\n"
"After collecting all my personal data — including Telegram chats, voice "
"call transcripts, Google Photos, Google Drive documents, everything somehow "
"related to me — I stared at the progress bar with a kind smile. My dog "
"barked in the background, demanding attention. I ignored him, eyes fixed on "
"the screen.\n"
"\n"
"The kind smile disappeared when I got the extrapolation result.\n"
"\n"
"> “You, Alex, will be fired tomorrow,” the screen read.\n"
"\n"
"That had to be wrong. I repeat, I’m not a talented developer and not the "
"best one — but when the company struggles with something, they ask for my "
"help. I did a lot for them. I’m important to them. It was ridiculous.\n"
"\n"
"Ridiculous or not, that day I finished my task and sent the results "
"immediately after. The rest of the day I spent in my apartment in a "
"beautiful neighborhood somewhere in Warsaw — with a slightly greenish face.\n"
"\n"
"*\"This is ridiculous,\"* I kept hearing in my head.\n"
"\n"
"*“Listen, Alex, I like you…”* — that’s how my manager started the "
"conversation the next day.\n"
"\n"
"He listed what I had done for them, what the company was doing, that they "
"had to reduce spending, that they really appreciated my work — and many "
"other bullshit epithets.\n"
"\n"
"*“So we've decided to pause your working relationship for a while and focus "
"on company survival.”* — that’s how he finished.\n"
"\n"
"That was not funny at all. It took me three days to accept it. At least I "
"had good savings — and that creepy piece of software.\n"
"\n"
"After three days of staring at the ceiling, I came back to the software. "
"What else could I do? I was unemployed, emotionally bruised, and curious.\n"
"\n"
"I opened the extrapolation interface and typed:\n"
"\n"
"> “What if we didn’t get a dog one year ago?”\n"
"\n"
"Result: In 99.9% of variations — we still got a dog. Just later.  \n"
"Sometimes it’s a whippet. Sometimes it’s a mutt. In one rare case, we got a "
"cat. The cat ran away in six months.\n"
"\n"
"Next test:  \n"
"\n"
"> “What if I won the lottery?”\n"
"\n"
"Great news — I did. Once or twice in different timelines. And then I lost "
"it all on real estate in Italy or shady crypto startups. No happiness was "
"detected.\n"
"\n"
"And then I grew bolder.\n"
"\n"
"I asked the real question — the one I had always wanted to know the answer "
"to:\n"
"\n"
"> “What if I won the programming olympiads 15 years ago?”\n"
"\n"
"Result: life shift. Massive.\n"
"\n"
"That version of me entered a top university in another country. He made "
"friends — actual friends, with opinions and a taste in architecture. He "
"co-founded a machine learning startup before I even learned how to hold eye "
"contact in interviews.\n"
"\n"
"And weirdest of all — he seemed… happy?\n"
"\n"
"I scrolled through his life logs. He drank smoothies in Palo Alto. He "
"surfed. He pitched to venture capitalists and got rejected. Then he pitched "
"again. Eventually, he failed gracefully.\n"
"\n"
"![img.png](/blog/dog/polo.webp)\n"
"\n"
"He dated people I couldn't even imagine existing. He read poetry. He even "
"had a therapist.\n"
"\n"
"But the strangest part? Near the end of his timeline, he left a private "
"note in the system:\n"
"\n"
"> “Sometimes I wonder what my life would’ve been like if I stayed in "
"Poland. Maybe in a small apartment in Warsaw. Maybe walking a dog. I think "
"I’d like that too.”\n"
"\n"
"That’s when I closed the laptop.\n"
"\n"
"I didn’t touch the software for a week. I went on long walks. Listened to "
"music without skipping every 30 seconds.\n"
"\n"
"All the timelines, all the versions of me, all the simulations — they "
"echoed in my head like reruns of a show I’d already watched.\n"
"\n"
"I realized that the drastic changes made me unrecognizable. They weren’t me "
"— just projections. Branches growing in every direction, but from a root I "
"barely remembered planting.\n"
"\n"
"I opened the app one last time.  \n"
"Final prompt:  \n"
"\n"
"> “What if I don’t ask anymore?”\n"
"\n"
"The system froze. Then replied:  \n"
"\n"
"> “No projections available.”\n"
"\n"
"Good.\n"
"\n"
"I shut the laptop down and archived the logs.\n"
"\n"
"The dog stared at me. He usually does that when it’s time for a walk — at 3 "
"p.m.\n"
"\n"
"And for the first time in weeks, I didn’t want to be anywhere else.\n"
"\n"
"![img.png](/blog/dog/dog-park2.webp)\n"
msgstr ""
"Saya bukanlah seorang pembangun perisian berbakat. Saya bukan yang paling "
"pantas — dan pastinya bukan yang terbaik. Tetapi apabila syarikat tempat "
"saya bekerja menghadapi masalah dengan sesuatu yang penting dan mendesak, "
"mereka meminta bantuan saya dan membayar saya banyak. Tidak tahu kenapa.\n"
"\n"
"Syarikat ini membuat chatbot untuk hiburan. Anda tahu iklan seperti *\"Mari "
"berbual dengan Albert Einstein\"* atau *\"Mari berbual dengan Marilyn "
"Monroe.\"* Yang saya rasa agak bodoh — tetapi ia berkesan. Ya, ia pernah "
"berkesan, untuk lebih tepat. Syarikat itu terperangkap. Tiada idea untuk "
"ciri baharu, tiada watak menarik. Sesiapa yang ingin mencubanya sudah pun "
"mencuba. Pendapatan semakin merosot. Penulis pasukan, yang diambil untuk "
"mencipta persona sebegitu, tidak dapat mengekalkan kualiti, dan kualiti "
"semakin merosot.\n"
"\n"
"Tugas kami adalah untuk memperbaikinya — tanpa idea yang nyata bagaimana. "
"Itulah sahaja yang anda perlu tahu tentang pengurusan dan proses majikan "
"saya, atau kekurangan proses, visi, pelan, tanggungjawab. Tetapi baiklah.\n"
"\n"
"![img.png](/blog/dog/monroe.webp)\n"
"\n"
"Idea penulis adalah untuk mencipta seorang tokoh terkenal yang telah "
"mencuba kehidupan lain — jadi pengguna boleh berbual, sebagai contoh, "
"dengan Donald Trump, yang di pertengahan kehidupannya memutuskan untuk "
"menukar kerjaya dan menjadi pelukis. Mungkin penulis kami mendapat "
"inspirasi dari Donald yang baru-baru ini mengumumkan lukisan, kononnya "
"dihantar kepada Epstein. Tetapi bagaimanapun. Penulis memberikan saya draf "
"satu muka surat tentang kehidupan Donald selepas perubahan kerjayanya.\n"
"\n"
"Yang mana tidak cukup untuk mencipta persona AI yang baik. Saya memerlukan "
"sekurang-kurangnya 20 muka surat teks untuk mengisi stor vektor QDrant "
"kami, jadi sistem AI RAG boleh dengan bebas memilih dokumen yang terbenam "
"dengan baik untuk proses penalaan yang sesuai. *Maaf untuk istilah "
"kejuruteraan.*\n"
"\n"
"Selepas satu hari menunggu, saya memutuskan untuk menggunakan AI untuk "
"menghasilkan apa yang mungkin ditulis oleh penulis kami. Ia adalah satu "
"tindakan prokrastinasi. Saya cuma mahu mengisi masa menunggu. Mengejutkan, "
"hasilnya hampir sama dengan apa yang penulis berikan kepada saya. Jujur, "
"itu mengejutkan saya.\n"
"\n"
"Ia mungkin kebetulan, jadi saya ingin memeriksanya semula dengan data "
"sebenar — dengan data peribadi saya. Kemudian, saya menyedari bahawa itu "
"adalah keputusan yang salah.\n"
"\n"
"Syarikat berada dalam keadaan terdesak. *\"Kita perlukan persona ini siap "
"semalam,\"* kata pengasas. Saya ragu bahawa persona ini akan menyegarkan "
"syarikat. Saya meminta dua hari tambahan untuk menyiapkan kerja saya. "
"Kebanyakan masa saya rancang untuk dialokasikan kepada eksperimen saya.\n"
"\n"
"Selepas mengumpulkan semua data peribadi saya — termasuk sembang Telegram, "
"transkrip panggilan suara, Google Photos, dokumen Google Drive, "
"segala-galanya yang agak berkaitan dengan saya — saya merenung bar progres "
"dengan senyuman yang lembut. Anjing saya menyalak di latar belakang, "
"menuntut perhatian. Saya mengabaikannya, mata terkunci pada skrin.\n"
"\n"
"Senayuman lembut itu hilang apabila saya mendapat hasil ekstrapolasi.\n"
"\n"
"> “Anda, Alex, akan dipecat esok,” baca skrin.\n"
"\n"
"Itu pasti salah. Saya ulang, saya bukan pembangun berbakat dan bukan yang "
"terbaik — tetapi bila syarikat menghadapi masalah dengan sesuatu, mereka "
"minta bantuan saya. Saya banyak berbuat untuk mereka. Saya penting kepada "
"mereka. Ia adalah mengarut.\n"
"\n"
"Mengarut atau tidak, hari itu saya menyelesaikan tugas saya dan menghantar "
"keputusan sejurus selepasnya. Sepanjang hari saya habiskan di apartmen saya "
"di kawasan kejiranan yang indah di Warsaw — dengan muka yang sedikit hijau.\n"
"\n"
"*\"Ini mengarut,\"* saya terus mendengar dalam kepala saya.\n"
"\n"
"*“Dengar, Alex, saya suka awak…”* — itulah cara pengurus saya memulakan "
"perbualan pada keesokan harinya.\n"
"\n"
"Dia menyenaraikan apa yang telah saya lakukan untuk mereka, apa yang "
"syarikat lakukan, mereka perlu mengurangkan perbelanjaan, mereka "
"benar-benar menghargai kerja saya — dan banyak epithet yang tidak "
"menyenangkan.\n"
"\n"
"*“Jadi kami memutuskan untuk menghentikan hubungan kerja anda buat "
"sementara waktu dan fokus pada kelangsungan hidup syarikat.”* — itulah cara "
"dia mengakhiri.\n"
"\n"
"Itu tidak lucu langsung. Saya memerlukan tiga hari untuk menerimanya. "
"Sekurang-kurangnya saya mempunyai simpanan yang baik — dan perisian yang "
"menyeramkan itu.\n"
"\n"
"Setelah tiga hari menatap siling, saya kembali kepada perisian. Apa lagi "
"yang boleh saya lakukan? Saya menganggur, secara emosional terluka, dan "
"ingin tahu.\n"
"\n"
"Saya membuka antara muka ekstrapolasi dan menaip:\n"
"\n"
"> “Bagaimana jika kita tidak mendapatkan anjing setahun yang lalu?”\n"
"\n"
"Hasilnya: Dalam 99.9% variasi — kita tetap mendapatkan anjing. Cuma lebih "
"lambat. Kadang-kadang ia adalah whippet. Kadang-kadang ia adalah anjing "
"kacukan. Dalam satu kes yang jarang berlaku, kita mendapatkan kucing. "
"Kucing itu lari selepas enam bulan.\n"
"\n"
"Ujian seterusnya:  \n"
"\n"
"> “Bagaimana jika saya menang loteri?”\n"
"\n"
"Berita baik — saya menang. Sekali atau dua kali dalam garis masa yang "
"berbeza. Dan kemudian saya kehilangannya semua pada hartanah di Itali atau "
"startup crypto yang mencurigakan. Tiada kebahagiaan dikesan.\n"
"\n"
"Kemudian saya menjadi lebih berani.\n"
"\n"
"Saya bertanyakan soalan sebenar — yang selalu saya ingin tahu jawabannya:\n"
"\n"
"> “Bagaimana jika saya memenangi olimpiad pengaturcaraan 15 tahun lalu?”\n"
"\n"
"Hasilnya: perubahan hidup. Besar.\n"
"\n"
"Versi saya itu memasuki universiti terkemuka di negara lain. Dia membuat "
"kawan — kawan sebenar dengan pendapat dan minat dalam seni bina. Dia "
"menubuhkan startup pembelajaran mesin sebelum saya pun belajar bagaimana "
"untuk menahan kontak mata dalam temuduga.\n"
"\n"
"Dan yang paling pelik sekali — dia kelihatan... gembira?\n"
"\n"
"Saya menyemak log kehidupannya. Dia minum smoothie di Palo Alto. Dia "
"berselancar. Dia membuat pitch kepada kapitalis teroka dan ditolak. "
"Kemudian dia pitch lagi. Akhirnya, dia gagal dengan anggun.\n"
"\n"
"![img.png](/blog/dog/polo.webp)\n"
"\n"
"Dia berkenalan dengan orang yang saya tidak dapat bayangkan wujud. Dia "
"membaca puisi. Dia malah mempunyai seorang terapis.\n"
"\n"
"Tetapi bahagian yang paling pelik? Dekat akhir garis masanya, dia "
"meninggalkan catatan peribadi dalam sistem:\n"
"\n"
"> “Kadang-kadang saya tertanya-tanya bagaimana hidup saya akan jika saya "
"tetap di Poland. Mungkin di apartmen kecil di Warsaw. Mungkin "
"berjalan-jalan dengan anjing. Saya rasa saya juga akan suka itu.”\n"
"\n"
"Ketika itulah saya menutup laptop.\n"
"\n"
"Saya tidak menyentuh perisian selama seminggu. Saya pergi berjalan-jalan "
"jauh. Mendengar muzik tanpa melangkau setiap 30 saat.\n"
"\n"
"Semua garis masa, semua versi diri saya, semua simulasi — mereka bergema "
"dalam kepala saya seperti ulangan rancangan yang telah saya tonton.\n"
"\n"
"Saya menyedari bahawa perubahan drastik membuat saya tidak dikenali. Mereka "
"bukan saya — hanya unjuran. Cabang-cabang yang tumbuh dalam setiap arah, "
"tetapi dari akar yang saya hampir tidak ingat menanamnya.\n"
"\n"
"Saya membuka aplikasi satu kali terakhir.  \n"
"Dorongan terakhir:  \n"
"\n"
"> “Bagaimana jika saya tidak bertanya lagi?”\n"
"\n"
"Sistem terhenti. Kemudian menjawab: \n"
"\n"
"> “Tiada unjuran tersedia.”\n"
"\n"
"Bagus.\n"
"\n"
"Saya menutup laptop dan mengarkibkan log.\n"
"\n"
"Anjing itu merenung saya. Dia biasanya melakukan itu apabila tiba masanya "
"untuk berjalan-jalan — pada 3 petang.\n"
"\n"
"Dan untuk pertama kali dalam minggu ini, saya tidak mahu berada di tempat "
"lain.\n"
"\n"
"![img.png](/blog/dog/dog-park2.webp)"

