#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "Shopping"
msgstr "Pembelian"

#: src/features/RolePlay/scenarios/at-the-grocery-store.ts:16
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid ""
"Shopping at a grocery store involves many short but useful conversations. "
"You may need to find a product, ask about a price, understand a promotion, "
"check ingredients, or speak with a cashier.\n"
"\n"
"You do not need long or complicated sentences. Clear questions and polite "
"phrases are usually enough.\n"
"\n"
"## How to Ask Where Something Is\n"
"\n"
"When you cannot find a product, you can approach an employee and say:\n"
"\n"
"- “Excuse me, could you help me?”\n"
"- “Where can I find the milk?”\n"
"- “Which aisle is the pasta in?”\n"
"- “Do you know where the rice is?”\n"
"- “I’m looking for olive oil.”\n"
"- “Could you show me where it is?”\n"
"\n"
"An employee may respond with directions such as:\n"
"\n"
"- “It’s in aisle five.”\n"
"- “It’s next to the bread.”\n"
"- “You’ll find it at the back of the store.”\n"
"- “It’s on the top shelf.”\n"
"- “It’s in the refrigerated section.”\n"
"- “Follow me. I’ll show you.”\n"
"\n"
"Useful location words include:\n"
"\n"
"- **Aisle** — a passage between shelves\n"
"- **Shelf** — the surface where products are displayed\n"
"- **Checkout** — the place where you pay\n"
"- **Refrigerated section** — the area for chilled products\n"
"- **Frozen-food section** — the area containing frozen products\n"
"- **Produce section** — the area containing fruit and vegetables\n"
"- **Bakery section** — the area containing bread and baked goods\n"
"\n"
"## Ask Whether a Product Is Available\n"
"\n"
"Sometimes a shelf is empty or the product you need is difficult to find.\n"
"\n"
"You can ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Do you have this product?”\n"
"- “Do you sell oat milk?”\n"
"- “Is this item still available?”\n"
"- “Do you have any more in stock?”\n"
"- “When will this be available again?”\n"
"- “Is there another brand you would recommend?”\n"
"- “Do you have a similar product?”\n"
"\n"
"If the product is unavailable, an employee may say:\n"
"\n"
"- “I’m afraid it’s out of stock.”\n"
"- “We should have more tomorrow.”\n"
"- “That product has been discontinued.”\n"
"- “We have a similar one from another brand.”\n"
"- “Let me check in the storage room.”\n"
"\n"
"## Ask About Prices\n"
"\n"
"Price labels can sometimes be unclear, especially when several products are "
"displayed together.\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “How much is this?”\n"
"- “Could you check the price for me?”\n"
"- “Is this the correct price?”\n"
"- “Is the price per item or per kilogram?”\n"
"- “Does this include tax?”\n"
"- “Why is the price different at the checkout?”\n"
"- “Which one is cheaper?”\n"
"\n"
"You may also hear:\n"
"\n"
"- “It costs three ninety-nine.”\n"
"- “It’s sold by weight.”\n"
"- “The price is per kilogram.”\n"
"- “The discount is applied at the checkout.”\n"
"- “You need a loyalty card to get that price.”\n"
"\n"
"## Understand Promotions and Discounts\n"
"\n"
"Stores often use promotional language that may be confusing.\n"
"\n"
"Common offers include:\n"
"\n"
"- **Buy one, get one free**\n"
"- **Two for five**\n"
"- **Twenty percent off**\n"
"- **Reduced price**\n"
"- **Special offer**\n"
"- **Member price**\n"
"- **Loyalty-card price**\n"
"- **Clearance**\n"
"- **Valid until Friday**\n"
"\n"
"Questions you can ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Is this product on sale?”\n"
"- “How does this promotion work?”\n"
"- “Do I need to buy two?”\n"
"- “Do I need a loyalty card?”\n"
"- “Is the discount applied automatically?”\n"
"- “When does the promotion end?”\n"
"- “Can I combine this offer with another discount?”\n"
"\n"
"For example:\n"
"\n"
"> “The label says two for five. Can I buy only one?”\n"
"\n"
"The employee may explain:\n"
"\n"
"> “Yes, but one item will cost three.”\n"
"\n"
"## Compare Products\n"
"\n"
"You may want to compare brands, sizes, ingredients, or prices.\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “What is the difference between these two?”\n"
"- “Which one is more popular?”\n"
"- “Which one is better value?”\n"
"- “Is there a cheaper option?”\n"
"- “Do you have a larger size?”\n"
"- “Does this come in a smaller package?”\n"
"- “Which brand would you recommend?”\n"
"- “Is there a store-brand version?”\n"
"\n"
"A useful phrase is:\n"
"\n"
"> “I’m looking for something similar, but less expensive.”\n"
"\n"
"You can also explain your priorities:\n"
"\n"
"- “I need something without added sugar.”\n"
"- “I’m looking for a high-protein option.”\n"
"- “I’d prefer something organic.”\n"
"- “I need a product that will last several days.”\n"
"- “I’m looking for the best value, not necessarily the cheapest product.”\n"
"\n"
"## Ask About Ingredients and Dietary Needs\n"
"\n"
"Checking ingredients is especially important if you have allergies or "
"dietary preferences.\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Does this contain nuts?”\n"
"- “Is this gluten-free?”\n"
"- “Is this suitable for vegetarians?”\n"
"- “Is this vegan?”\n"
"- “Does this contain dairy?”\n"
"- “Is there any added sugar?”\n"
"- “Where can I find lactose-free products?”\n"
"- “Do you have a dairy-free alternative?”\n"
"\n"
"You can also say:\n"
"\n"
"- “I’m allergic to peanuts.”\n"
"- “I cannot eat gluten.”\n"
"- “I’m looking for something without dairy.”\n"
"- “Could you help me check the ingredients?”\n"
"\n"
"For serious allergies, always read the package carefully. A store employee "
"may help you find information, but they may not be able to guarantee that a "
"product is completely allergen-free.\n"
"\n"
"## Buy Fruit, Vegetables, Meat, or Cheese\n"
"\n"
"Some products are sold by weight rather than by package.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “I’d like one kilogram of apples, please.”\n"
"- “Could I have half a kilogram of tomatoes?”\n"
"- “I’d like three hundred grams of cheese.”\n"
"- “Could you give me six slices?”\n"
"- “Can I have two chicken breasts?”\n"
"- “That’s enough, thank you.”\n"
"\n"
"The employee may ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “How much would you like?”\n"
"- “Is this amount okay?”\n"
"- “Would you like it sliced?”\n"
"- “Would you like anything else?”\n"
"- “Do you need a bag?”\n"
"\n"
"You can respond:\n"
"\n"
"- “A little more, please.”\n"
"- “A little less, please.”\n"
"- “That amount is perfect.”\n"
"- “Could you slice it thinly?”\n"
"- “No, that’s everything.”\n"
"\n"
"## Ask About Product Freshness\n"
"\n"
"You may want to check whether food is fresh or how long it will last.\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “When does this expire?”\n"
"- “What is the use-by date?”\n"
"- “Was this baked today?”\n"
"- “Is this fresh?”\n"
"- “How long will this keep?”\n"
"- “Should I store this in the refrigerator?”\n"
"- “Can this be frozen?”\n"
"\n"
"Common date labels include:\n"
"\n"
"- **Best before** — the product may lose quality after this date\n"
"- **Use by** — the product should normally be consumed before this date\n"
"- **Packed on** — the date the product was packaged\n"
"- **Sell by** — a date mainly used by the store\n"
"\n"
"## Handle Problems with a Product\n"
"\n"
"You may notice that an item is damaged, open, expired, or incorrectly "
"labelled.\n"
"\n"
"You can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “This package is damaged.”\n"
"- “This bottle is leaking.”\n"
"- “I think this product has expired.”\n"
"- “The seal is broken.”\n"
"- “This item was on the wrong shelf.”\n"
"- “Could I exchange this for another one?”\n"
"- “Could someone check this product?”\n"
"\n"
"Stay polite and explain the problem clearly.\n"
"\n"
"For example:\n"
"\n"
"> “Excuse me, this carton is leaking. Could I replace it?”\n"
"\n"
"## Speak at the Checkout\n"
"\n"
"When you reach the checkout, the cashier may ask several common questions:\n"
"\n"
"- “Did you find everything you needed?”\n"
"- “Do you have a loyalty card?”\n"
"- “Would you like a bag?”\n"
"- “Do you need a receipt?”\n"
"- “Are you paying by cash or card?”\n"
"- “Would you like to donate to charity?”\n"
"- “Do you need help packing?”\n"
"\n"
"Useful answers include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Yes, I found everything, thank you.”\n"
"- “No, I couldn’t find one item.”\n"
"- “I don’t have a loyalty card.”\n"
"- “Yes, one bag, please.”\n"
"- “No bag, thank you.”\n"
"- “I’ll pay by card.”\n"
"- “Could I have the receipt, please?”\n"
"- “Could I pay separately for these items?”\n"
"\n"
"## Understand Checkout Instructions\n"
"\n"
"When paying by card, you may hear:\n"
"\n"
"- “Please insert your card.”\n"
"- “You can tap your card.”\n"
"- “Please enter your PIN.”\n"
"- “Your payment was declined.”\n"
"- “Would you like to try again?”\n"
"- “Please remove your card.”\n"
"- “The payment has gone through.”\n"
"\n"
"If something goes wrong, you can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could I try another card?”\n"
"- “Can I pay in cash instead?”\n"
"- “I think I was charged twice.”\n"
"- “Could you check the total?”\n"
"- “The price on the shelf was different.”\n"
"- “Could you remove this item, please?”\n"
"\n"
"## Use Self-Checkout\n"
"\n"
"At a self-checkout, you may need to ask an employee for help.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could you help me with the self-checkout?”\n"
"- “The machine is not scanning this item.”\n"
"- “It says there is an unexpected item.”\n"
"- “How do I weigh the vegetables?”\n"
"- “Where do I enter the product number?”\n"
"- “How can I remove an item?”\n"
"- “The machine has not printed my receipt.”\n"
"\n"
"You may see or hear instructions such as:\n"
"\n"
"- “Scan your first item.”\n"
"- “Place the item in the bagging area.”\n"
"- “Select your payment method.”\n"
"- “Approval needed.”\n"
"- “Please wait for assistance.”\n"
"\n"
"## A Simple Grocery Store Conversation\n"
"\n"
"A typical interaction may look like this:\n"
"\n"
"> **Customer:** Excuse me, could you help me find oat milk?  \n"
"> **Employee:** Of course. It’s in aisle six, next to the regular milk.  \n"
"> **Customer:** Thank you. Do you have an unsweetened version?  \n"
"> **Employee:** Yes, we have two brands. This one is currently on sale.  \n"
"> **Customer:** How does the promotion work?  \n"
"> **Employee:** It’s twenty percent off if you have a loyalty card.  \n"
"> **Customer:** I don’t have one. Is there a cheaper alternative?  \n"
"> **Employee:** Yes, the store-brand version is less expensive.  \n"
"> **Customer:** Great. Could you show me where it is?\n"
"\n"
"## A Simple Shopping Formula\n"
"\n"
"When you need help, use this structure:\n"
"\n"
"1. **Get attention:** “Excuse me, could you help me?”\n"
"2. **Explain what you need:** “I’m looking for brown rice.”\n"
"3. **Ask a specific question:** “Which aisle is it in?”\n"
"4. **Clarify the answer:** “Did you say aisle seven?”\n"
"5. **Thank the employee:** “Great, thank you for your help.”\n"
"\n"
"## Practice Scenario\n"
"\n"
"In this roleplay, you are shopping at FreshMart. The AI employee will help "
"you find products, explain prices and promotions, and answer questions "
"about the store.\n"
"\n"
"During the conversation, try to:\n"
"\n"
"- Ask where at least one product is located.\n"
"- Ask about a price or promotion.\n"
"- Compare two products.\n"
"- Ask about an ingredient or dietary requirement.\n"
"- Respond to one small problem, such as an unavailable product or unclear "
"price.\n"
"- Complete the purchase or end the interaction politely.\n"
"\n"
"Focus on communicating your needs clearly. You do not need perfect grammar "
"to have a successful conversation in a grocery store."
msgstr ""
"Berbelanja di kedai runcit melibatkan banyak perbualan pendek tetapi "
"berguna. Anda mungkin perlu mencari produk, bertanya tentang harga, "
"memahami promosi, memeriksa ramuan, atau bercakap dengan juruwang.\n"
"\n"
"Anda tidak memerlukan ayat yang panjang atau rumit. Soalan yang jelas dan "
"frasa yang sopan biasanya mencukupi.\n"
"\n"
"## Bagaimana untuk Bertanya Di Mana Sesuatu\n"
"\n"
"Apabila anda tidak dapat mencari produk, anda boleh mendekati seorang "
"pekerja dan berkata:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Maaf, bolehkah anda membantu saya?\"\n"
"- \"Di mana saya boleh mencari susu?\"\n"
"- \"Laluan mana pasta berada?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda tahu di mana beras?\"\n"
"- \"Saya mencari minyak zaitun.\"\n"
"- \"Bolehkah anda tunjukkan saya di mana ia berada?\"\n"
"\n"
"Pekerja mungkin memberi respons dengan arahan seperti:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Ia di lorong lima.\"\n"
"- \"Ia bersebelahan dengan roti.\"\n"
"- \"Anda akan menemukannya di belakang kedai.\"\n"
"- \"Ia di rak atas.\"\n"
"- \"Ia di bahagian yang sejuk.\"\n"
"- \"Ikut saya. Saya akan tunjukkan.\"\n"
"\n"
"Kata lokasi berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- **Lorong** — laluan di antara rak\n"
"- **Rak** — permukaan tempat produk dipamerkan\n"
"- **Kaunter** — tempat di mana anda membayar\n"
"- **Bahagian sejuk** — kawasan untuk produk sejuk\n"
"- **Bahagian makanan beku** — kawasan yang mengandungi produk beku\n"
"- **Bahagian hasil** — kawasan yang mengandungi buah-buahan dan sayuran\n"
"- **Bahagian roti** — kawasan yang mengandungi roti dan barang bakar\n"
"\n"
"## Bertanya Sama Ada Produk Tersedia\n"
"\n"
"Kadang-kadang rak kosong atau produk yang anda perlukan sukar untuk "
"dijumpai.\n"
"\n"
"Anda boleh bertanya:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda mempunyai produk ini?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda menjual susu oat?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah item ini masih tersedia?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda mempunyai lebih banyak dalam stok?\"\n"
"- \"Bilakah ia akan tersedia lagi?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah terdapat jenama lain yang anda syorkan?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda mempunyai produk yang serupa?\"\n"
"\n"
"Jika produk tidak tersedia, seorang pekerja mungkin berkata:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Saya takut ia sudah kehabisan stok.\"\n"
"- \"Kami akan ada lebih banyak esok.\"\n"
"- \"Produk itu telah dihentikan.\"\n"
"- \"Kami mempunyai yang serupa dari jenama lain.\"\n"
"- \"Biar saya periksa di bilik simpanan.\"\n"
"\n"
"## Bertanya Tentang Harga\n"
"\n"
"Label harga kadang-kadang boleh tidak jelas, terutamanya apabila beberapa "
"produk dipamerkan bersama.\n"
"\n"
"Soalan berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Berapa harga ini?\"\n"
"- \"Bolehkah anda periksa harga untuk saya?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah ini harga yang betul?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah harga ini per item atau per kilogram?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah ini termasuk cukai?\"\n"
"- \"Mengapa harga berbeza di kaunter?\"\n"
"- \"Mana yang lebih murah?\"\n"
"\n"
"Anda mungkin juga mendengar:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Ia berharga tiga sembilan puluh sembilan.\"\n"
"- \"Ia dijual mengikut berat.\"\n"
"- \"Harga adalah per kilogram.\"\n"
"- \"Diskaun dikenakan di kaunter.\"\n"
"- \"Anda memerlukan kad kesetiaan untuk mendapatkan harga tersebut.\"\n"
"\n"
"## Memahami Promosi dan Diskaun\n"
"\n"
"Kedai sering menggunakan bahasa promosi yang mungkin membingungkan.\n"
"\n"
"Tawaran biasa termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- **Beli satu, percuma satu**\n"
"- **Dua untuk lima**\n"
"- **Dua puluh peratus diskaun**\n"
"- **Harga dikurangkan**\n"
"- **Tawaran istimewa**\n"
"- **Harga ahli**\n"
"- **Harga kad kesetiaan**\n"
"- **Jualan besar-besaran**\n"
"- **Sah sehingga Jumaat**\n"
"\n"
"Soalan yang boleh anda tanya:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Adakah produk ini dalam jualan?\"\n"
"- \"Bagaimana promosi ini berfungsi?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah saya perlu membeli dua?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah saya memerlukan kad kesetiaan?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah diskaun dikenakan secara automatik?\"\n"
"- \"Bilakah promosi ini berakhir?\"\n"
"- \"Bolehkah saya menggabungkan tawaran ini dengan diskaun lain?\"\n"
"\n"
"Sebagai contoh:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Label mengatakan dua untuk lima. Bolehkah saya beli hanya satu?\"\n"
"\n"
"Pekerja mungkin menerangkan:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Ya, tetapi satu item akan berharga tiga.\"\n"
"\n"
"## Membandingkan Produk\n"
"\n"
"Anda mungkin mahu membandingkan jenama, saiz, bahan, atau harga.\n"
"\n"
"Soalan berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Apakah perbezaan antara kedua-dua ini?\"\n"
"- \"Mana yang lebih popular?\"\n"
"- \"Mana yang lebih bernilai?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah terdapat pilihan yang lebih murah?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda mempunyai saiz yang lebih besar?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah ini datang dalam pakej yang lebih kecil?\"\n"
"- \"Jenama mana yang anda syorkan?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah terdapat versi jenama kedai?\"\n"
"\n"
"Frasa berguna ialah:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Saya mencari sesuatu yang serupa, tetapi kurang mahal.\"\n"
"\n"
"Anda juga boleh menjelaskan keutamaan anda:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Saya perlukan sesuatu tanpa gula tambahan.\"\n"
"- \"Saya mencari pilihan protein tinggi.\"\n"
"- \"Saya lebih suka sesuatu yang organik.\"\n"
"- \"Saya perlukan produk yang tahan beberapa hari.\"\n"
"- \"Saya mencari nilai terbaik, bukan semestinya produk paling murah.\"\n"
"\n"
"## Bertanya Tentang Bahan dan Keperluan Pemakanan\n"
"\n"
"Memeriksa bahan adalah penting terutamanya jika anda mempunyai alahan atau "
"keutamaan pemakanan.\n"
"\n"
"Soalan berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Adakah ini mengandungi kacang?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah ini bebas gluten?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah ini sesuai untuk vegetarian?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah ini vegan?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah ini mengandungi produk tenusu?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah terdapat gula tambahan?\"\n"
"- \"Di mana saya boleh temui produk bebas laktosa?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda mempunyai alternatif bebas tenusu?\"\n"
"\n"
"Anda juga boleh berkata:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Saya alah kepada kacang.\"\n"
"- \"Saya tidak boleh makan gluten.\"\n"
"- \"Saya mencari sesuatu tanpa produk tenusu.\"\n"
"- \"Bolehkah anda bantu saya memeriksa bahan?\"\n"
"\n"
"Untuk alahan serius, selalu baca bungkusan dengan teliti. Pekerja kedai "
"mungkin membantu anda mencari maklumat, tetapi mereka mungkin tidak dapat "
"menjamin bahawa produk tersebut benar-benar bebas alergen.\n"
"\n"
"## Membeli Buah, Sayur, Daging, atau Keju\n"
"\n"
"Beberapa produk dijual mengikut berat daripada pakej.\n"
"\n"
"Frasa berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Saya mahu satu kilogram epal, tolong.\"\n"
"- \"Bolehkah saya mempunyai setengah kilogram tomato?\"\n"
"- \"Saya mahu tiga ratus gram keju.\"\n"
"- \"Bolehkah anda beri saya enam keping?\"\n"
"- \"Bolehkah saya dapatkan dua dada ayam?\"\n"
"- \"Cukup, terima kasih.\"\n"
"\n"
"Pekerja mungkin bertanya:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Berapa banyak yang anda mahu?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah jumlah ini okey?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda mahu ia dihiris?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda mahukan apa-apa lagi?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda perlukan beg?\"\n"
"\n"
"Anda boleh membalas:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Sedikit lebih, tolong.\"\n"
"- \"Sedikit kurang, tolong.\"\n"
"- \"Kuanta ini sempurna.\"\n"
"- \"Bolehkah anda hiris dengan nipis?\"\n"
"- \"Tidak, itu sahaja.\"\n"
"\n"
"## Bertanya Tentang Kesegaran Produk\n"
"\n"
"Anda mungkin mahu memeriksa sama ada makanan segar atau berapa lama ia akan "
"bertahan.\n"
"\n"
"Soalan berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Bila ini akan tamat tempoh?\"\n"
"- \"Apakah tarikh akhir penggunaan?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah ini dibakar hari ini?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah ini segar?\"\n"
"- \"Berapa lama ini boleh tahan?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah saya perlu simpan ini dalam peti sejuk?\"\n"
"- \"Bolehkah ini dibekukan?\"\n"
"\n"
"Label tarikh biasa termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- **Sebelum terbaik** — produk mungkin kehilangan kualiti selepas tarikh "
"ini\n"
"- **Guna sebelum** — produk biasanya harus dimakan sebelum tarikh ini\n"
"- **Dibungkus pada** — tarikh produk dibungkus\n"
"- **Jual sebelum** — tarikh yang kebanyakan digunakan oleh kedai\n"
"\n"
"## Menangani Masalah dengan Produk\n"
"\n"
"Anda mungkin menyedari bahawa item rosak, terbuka, tamat tempoh, atau "
"dilabel secara salah.\n"
"\n"
"Anda boleh berkata:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Bungkusan ini rosak.\"\n"
"- \"Botol ini bocor.\"\n"
"- \"Saya rasa produk ini telah tamat tempoh.\"\n"
"- \"Penutupnya patah.\"\n"
"- \"Item ini berada di rak yang salah.\"\n"
"- \"Bolehkah saya tukar ini dengan yang lain?\"\n"
"- \"Bolehkah seseorang periksa produk ini?\"\n"
"\n"
"Jangan lupa untuk bersikap sopan dan jelaskan masalah dengan jelas.\n"
"\n"
"Sebagai contoh:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Maaf, karton ini bocor. Bolehkah saya gantikan ia?\"\n"
"\n"
"## Bercakap di Kaunter\n"
"\n"
"Apabila anda sampai ke kaunter, juruwang mungkin bertanya beberapa soalan "
"biasa:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda menemui semua yang diperlukan?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda mempunyai kad kesetiaan?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda mahu beg?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda perlukan resit?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda membayar secara tunai atau kad?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda mahu derma kepada amal?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda perlukan bantuan pembungkusan?\"\n"
"\n"
"Jawapan berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Ya, saya jumpa semua, terima kasih.\"\n"
"- \"Tidak, saya tidak dapat cari satu item.\"\n"
"- \"Saya tidak mempunyai kad kesetiaan.\"\n"
"- \"Ya, satu beg, tolong.\"\n"
"- \"Tiada beg, terima kasih.\"\n"
"- \"Saya bayar dengan kad.\"\n"
"- \"Bolehkah saya dapatkan resit, tolong?\"\n"
"- \"Bolehkah saya bayar secara berasingan untuk item-item ini?\"\n"
"\n"
"## Memahami Arahan di Kaunter\n"
"\n"
"Apabila membayar dengan kad, anda mungkin mendengar:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Sila masukkan kad anda.\"\n"
"- \"Anda boleh sentuh kad anda.\"\n"
"- \"Sila masukkan PIN anda.\"\n"
"- \"Pembayaran anda ditolak.\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda mahu cuba lagi?\"\n"
"- \"Sila keluarkan kad anda.\"\n"
"- \"Pembayaran telah berjaya.\"\n"
"\n"
"Jika sesuatu yang salah, anda boleh berkata:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Bolehkah saya cuba kad lain?\"\n"
"- \"Bolehkah saya bayar secara tunai?\"\n"
"- \"Saya rasa saya telah dicaj dua kali.\"\n"
"- \"Bolehkah anda periksa jumlah keseluruhan?\"\n"
"- \"Harga di rak berbeza.\"\n"
"- \"Bolehkah anda keluarkan item ini, tolong?\"\n"
"\n"
"## Menggunakan Pembayaran Sendiri\n"
"\n"
"Di kaunter pembayaran sendiri, anda mungkin perlu meminta bantuan pekerja.\n"
"\n"
"Frasa berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Bolehkah anda bantu saya dengan pembayaran sendiri?\"\n"
"- \"Mesin tidak mengimbas item ini.\"\n"
"- \"Ia mengatakan terdapat item yang tidak dijangka.\"\n"
"- \"Bagaimana cara untuk menimbang sayur?\"\n"
"- \"Di mana saya masukkan nombor produk?\"\n"
"- \"Bagaimana cara untuk keluarkan item?\"\n"
"- \"Mesin tidak mencetak resit saya.\"\n"
"\n"
"Anda mungkin melihat atau mendengar arahan seperti:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Imbas item pertama anda.\"\n"
"- \"Letakkan item di kawasan pembungkusan.\"\n"
"- \"Pilih kaedah pembayaran anda.\"\n"
"- \"Persetujuan diperlukan.\"\n"
"- \"Sila tunggu bantuan.\"\n"
"\n"
"## Perbualan Mudah di Kedai Runcit\n"
"\n"
"Interaksi biasa mungkin kelihatan seperti ini:\n"
"\n"
"> **Pelanggan:** Maaf, bolehkah anda bantu saya cari susu oat?  \n"
"> **Pekerja:** Sudah tentu. Ia di lorong enam, bersebelahan dengan susu "
"biasa.  \n"
"> **Pelanggan:** Terima kasih. Adakah anda mempunyai versi tanpa gula?  \n"
"> **Pekerja:** Ya, kami mempunyai dua jenama. Yang ini sedang dalam "
"tawaran.  \n"
"> **Pelanggan:** Bagaimana promosi ini berfungsi?  \n"
"> **Pekerja:** Ia dua puluh peratus diskaun jika anda mempunyai kad "
"kesetiaan.  \n"
"> **Pelanggan:** Saya tidak ada. Adakah terdapat alternatif yang lebih "
"murah?  \n"
"> **Pekerja:** Ya, versi jenama kedai lebih murah.  \n"
"> **Pelanggan:** Bagus. Bolehkah anda tunjukkan saya di mana ia berada?\n"
"\n"
"## Formula Mudah untuk Membeli-Belah\n"
"\n"
"Apabila anda memerlukan bantuan, gunakan struktur ini:\n"
"\n"
"1. **Dapatkan perhatian:** \"Maaf, bolehkah anda bantu saya?\"\n"
"2. **Terangkan apa yang anda perlu:** \"Saya mencari beras perang.\"\n"
"3. **Tanyakan soalan tertentu:** \"Laluan mana ia berada?\"\n"
"4. **Jelaskan jawapan:** \"Adakah anda kata lorong tujuh?\"\n"
"5. **Ucapkan terima kasih kepada pekerja:** \"Bagus, terima kasih atas "
"bantuan anda.\"\n"
"\n"
"## Senario Latihan\n"
"\n"
"Dalam permainan peranan ini, anda membeli-belah di FreshMart. Pekerja AI "
"akan membantu anda mencari produk, menerangkan harga dan promosi, dan "
"menjawab soalan tentang kedai.\n"
"\n"
"Semasa perbualan, cuba untuk:\n"
"\n"
"- Tanyakan di mana sekurang-kurangnya satu produk berada.\n"
"- Tanyakan tentang harga atau promosi.\n"
"- Bandingkan dua produk.\n"
"- Tanyakan tentang ramuan atau keperluan pemakanan.\n"
"- Tanggapi satu masalah kecil, seperti produk yang tidak tersedia atau "
"harga yang tidak jelas.\n"
"- Selesaikan pembelian atau tamatkan interaksi secara sopan.\n"
"\n"
"Fokus pada menyampaikan keperluan anda dengan jelas. Anda tidak memerlukan "
"tatabahasa yang sempurna untuk mempunyai perbualan yang berjaya di kedai "
"runcit."

