#: src/features/RolePlay/scenarios/talking-to-a-doctor.ts:16
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid ""
"Talking to a doctor can be difficult, especially when you need to describe "
"symptoms in another language. You may need to explain what you feel, when "
"the problem started, how serious it is, and how it affects your daily life.\n"
"\n"
"You do not need advanced medical vocabulary. Clear descriptions, specific "
"examples, and honest answers are usually more useful than trying to guess "
"the name of a condition.\n"
"\n"
"This roleplay is for language practice only. It cannot diagnose a medical "
"condition, recommend treatment, or replace professional medical care. If "
"you believe you may be experiencing a medical emergency, contact your local "
"emergency service.\n"
"\n"
"## Start the Consultation\n"
"\n"
"A doctor may begin by asking:\n"
"\n"
"- “What brings you in today?”\n"
"- “How can I help you?”\n"
"- “What seems to be the problem?”\n"
"- “Could you describe your symptoms?”\n"
"- “When did this begin?”\n"
"- “Have you experienced this before?”\n"
"\n"
"You can begin with a short summary:\n"
"\n"
"- “I’ve had a persistent cough for about a week.”\n"
"- “I’ve been experiencing pain in my lower back.”\n"
"- “I’ve been feeling unusually tired recently.”\n"
"- “I have a rash on my arm that is not improving.”\n"
"- “I’ve been getting headaches more often than usual.”\n"
"- “I’m here to discuss the results of my recent tests.”\n"
"- “I’m following up about a problem we discussed previously.”\n"
"\n"
"A useful opening structure is:\n"
"\n"
"> “I’ve been experiencing [symptom] for [length of time], and it is "
"[improving, getting worse, or staying the same].”\n"
"\n"
"For example:\n"
"\n"
"> “I’ve been experiencing pain in my right shoulder for about ten days, and "
"it seems to be getting worse.”\n"
"\n"
"## Describe Where the Problem Is\n"
"\n"
"Be as specific as possible about the location of pain or discomfort.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “The pain is in my lower back.”\n"
"- “It hurts on the right side of my chest.”\n"
"- “I feel discomfort behind my left knee.”\n"
"- “The pain starts in my neck and moves into my shoulder.”\n"
"- “The rash is mainly on my arms.”\n"
"- “My whole body feels sore.”\n"
"- “It is difficult to identify the exact location.”\n"
"- “The pain seems to move.”\n"
"\n"
"The doctor may ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Can you point to where it hurts?”\n"
"- “Is it on one side or both sides?”\n"
"- “Does the pain move anywhere else?”\n"
"- “Is the discomfort near the surface or deeper inside?”\n"
"- “Is the affected area sensitive to touch?”\n"
"\n"
"## Explain When It Started\n"
"\n"
"The doctor will often ask when the symptoms began and whether anything "
"happened beforehand.\n"
"\n"
"You can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “It started this morning.”\n"
"- “I first noticed it three days ago.”\n"
"- “The symptoms began gradually.”\n"
"- “It started suddenly while I was exercising.”\n"
"- “It began after I returned from a trip.”\n"
"- “I noticed it after starting a new medication.”\n"
"- “I woke up with the pain.”\n"
"- “I cannot remember exactly when it started.”\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions you may hear:\n"
"\n"
"- “Did it begin suddenly or gradually?”\n"
"- “What were you doing when it started?”\n"
"- “Did anything unusual happen beforehand?”\n"
"- “Have the symptoms changed since then?”\n"
"- “Was there an injury?”\n"
"\n"
"## Describe How It Feels\n"
"\n"
"Try to describe the sensation rather than only saying that something hurts.\n"
"\n"
"Pain or discomfort may feel:\n"
"\n"
"- Sharp\n"
"- Dull\n"
"- Burning\n"
"- Throbbing\n"
"- Stabbing\n"
"- Aching\n"
"- Cramping\n"
"- Tight\n"
"- Heavy\n"
"- Tingling\n"
"- Numb\n"
"- Itchy\n"
"- Sensitive\n"
"- Tender\n"
"\n"
"Examples:\n"
"\n"
"- “It feels like a dull ache.”\n"
"- “I sometimes feel a sharp pain.”\n"
"- “There is a burning sensation.”\n"
"- “My fingers feel numb.”\n"
"- “The area is itchy and sensitive.”\n"
"- “It feels like pressure rather than pain.”\n"
"- “My chest feels tight.”\n"
"- “I have a tingling sensation in my hand.”\n"
"\n"
"If you do not know the exact word, describe it in another way:\n"
"\n"
"> “It feels as if something is pressing on the area.”\n"
"\n"
"## Explain How Severe It Is\n"
"\n"
"A doctor may ask you to rate pain or discomfort on a scale from zero to "
"ten.\n"
"\n"
"- **Zero** means no pain.\n"
"- **Ten** means the worst pain you can imagine.\n"
"\n"
"You can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “The pain is about a four out of ten.”\n"
"- “It is mild most of the time.”\n"
"- “It becomes severe in the evening.”\n"
"- “It is uncomfortable, but I can still work.”\n"
"- “The pain is strong enough to wake me up.”\n"
"- “It is difficult to walk because of it.”\n"
"- “The symptoms interfere with my daily activities.”\n"
"\n"
"It is also helpful to explain what you can or cannot do:\n"
"\n"
"- “I can walk, but climbing stairs is painful.”\n"
"- “I cannot concentrate at work.”\n"
"- “I have difficulty sleeping.”\n"
"- “I can eat normally.”\n"
"- “I become tired after minor physical activity.”\n"
"- “I have had to stop exercising.”\n"
"\n"
"## Explain How Often It Happens\n"
"\n"
"Symptoms may be constant or may come and go.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “The pain is constant.”\n"
"- “It comes and goes.”\n"
"- “It happens several times a day.”\n"
"- “It usually lasts for about twenty minutes.”\n"
"- “The symptoms are worse in the morning.”\n"
"- “It happens mainly after eating.”\n"
"- “It only happens when I exercise.”\n"
"- “I feel better after resting.”\n"
"- “There does not seem to be a pattern.”\n"
"\n"
"The doctor may ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “How long does each episode last?”\n"
"- “Does it happen every day?”\n"
"- “Is it worse at a particular time?”\n"
"- “Does anything trigger it?”\n"
"- “Does anything make it better?”\n"
"\n"
"## Describe What Makes It Better or Worse\n"
"\n"
"Explain whether movement, food, rest, medication, or another factor changes "
"your symptoms.\n"
"\n"
"You can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “It gets worse when I move.”\n"
"- “The pain increases when I take a deep breath.”\n"
"- “It feels better after I rest.”\n"
"- “Heat seems to help.”\n"
"- “The symptoms are worse after meals.”\n"
"- “It improves when I lie down.”\n"
"- “Pain relief helped temporarily.”\n"
"- “Nothing seems to make a difference.”\n"
"- “The problem becomes worse when I am stressed.”\n"
"\n"
"Useful vocabulary:\n"
"\n"
"- **Trigger** — something that causes or worsens a symptom\n"
"- **Relieve** — make a symptom less severe\n"
"- **Aggravate** — make a symptom worse\n"
"\n"
"## Mention Other Symptoms\n"
"\n"
"The doctor may ask whether you have noticed any other changes.\n"
"\n"
"Common questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Do you have a fever?”\n"
"- “Have you felt sick or vomited?”\n"
"- “Have you noticed any swelling?”\n"
"- “Have you lost your appetite?”\n"
"- “Have you experienced dizziness?”\n"
"- “Are you short of breath?”\n"
"- “Have you had difficulty sleeping?”\n"
"- “Have you noticed any changes in your weight?”\n"
"- “Do you have any weakness or numbness?”\n"
"\n"
"You can respond:\n"
"\n"
"- “I also have a mild fever.”\n"
"- “I have felt dizzy a few times.”\n"
"- “There is some swelling around the area.”\n"
"- “I have not noticed any other symptoms.”\n"
"- “My appetite is normal.”\n"
"- “I have been sleeping poorly.”\n"
"- “I feel tired, but I do not have a fever.”\n"
"\n"
"Do not leave out a symptom because you think it is unrelated. The doctor "
"can decide whether it is relevant.\n"
"\n"
"## Explain What You Have Already Tried\n"
"\n"
"Tell the doctor whether you have taken medication, changed your routine, or "
"tried another solution.\n"
"\n"
"You can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “I have been resting.”\n"
"- “I tried an over-the-counter pain reliever.”\n"
"- “I used a cold compress.”\n"
"- “I stopped exercising for several days.”\n"
"- “I changed my diet, but it did not help.”\n"
"- “The medication helped for a few hours.”\n"
"- “I have not tried anything yet.”\n"
"- “I spoke with a pharmacist before making this appointment.”\n"
"\n"
"Be ready to explain:\n"
"\n"
"- What you used\n"
"- How much you used\n"
"- How often you used it\n"
"- Whether it helped\n"
"- Whether you noticed side effects\n"
"\n"
"Do not pretend to remember details that you do not know. You can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “I don’t remember the exact name.”\n"
"- “I can show you the package.”\n"
"- “I’m not sure about the dosage.”\n"
"- “I took it according to the instructions on the label.”\n"
"\n"
"## Discuss Current Medication\n"
"\n"
"The doctor may need to know about all medication and supplements you take.\n"
"\n"
"You can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “I take this medication every morning.”\n"
"- “I use an inhaler when necessary.”\n"
"- “I recently started taking a new prescription.”\n"
"- “I stopped taking it last week.”\n"
"- “I occasionally take an over-the-counter pain reliever.”\n"
"- “I’m not currently taking any medication.”\n"
"- “I have a list of my medications with me.”\n"
"\n"
"The doctor may ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “What dose do you take?”\n"
"- “How long have you been taking it?”\n"
"- “Who prescribed it?”\n"
"- “Have you missed any doses?”\n"
"- “Have you noticed any side effects?”\n"
"\n"
"Do not stop prescribed medication based only on a language-learning "
"simulation. Discuss medication changes with a qualified healthcare "
"professional.\n"
"\n"
"## Mention Allergies\n"
"\n"
"Tell the doctor about medication, food, or other allergies.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “I’m allergic to penicillin.”\n"
"- “I have a severe peanut allergy.”\n"
"- “This medication caused a rash in the past.”\n"
"- “I do not have any known allergies.”\n"
"- “I’m not sure whether it was an allergic reaction.”\n"
"- “I experienced swelling after taking that medicine.”\n"
"\n"
"The doctor may ask what happened during the reaction and how serious it "
"was.\n"
"\n"
"## Discuss Your Medical History\n"
"\n"
"The doctor may ask about previous illnesses, injuries, operations, or "
"similar symptoms.\n"
"\n"
"You can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “I had the same problem two years ago.”\n"
"- “I have a history of back problems.”\n"
"- “I had surgery five years ago.”\n"
"- “I was treated for this previously.”\n"
"- “I have not experienced this before.”\n"
"- “I have a long-term medical condition.”\n"
"- “I was recently in hospital.”\n"
"- “I have brought my previous test results.”\n"
"\n"
"You may also be asked about health conditions in your family:\n"
"\n"
"- “Does anyone in your family have a similar condition?”\n"
"- “Is there a family history of heart disease?”\n"
"- “Do any close relatives have diabetes?”\n"
"\n"
"You can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “My father has a similar condition.”\n"
"- “There is no known family history.”\n"
"- “I’m not sure.”\n"
"- “I would need to check.”\n"
"\n"
"## Answer Lifestyle Questions\n"
"\n"
"A doctor may ask about sleep, exercise, diet, alcohol, smoking, work, or "
"stress because these factors can affect health.\n"
"\n"
"You may hear:\n"
"\n"
"- “Do you smoke?”\n"
"- “How often do you exercise?”\n"
"- “How much alcohol do you drink?”\n"
"- “How have you been sleeping?”\n"
"- “Has anything changed in your diet?”\n"
"- “Are you under unusual stress?”\n"
"- “What kind of work do you do?”\n"
"\n"
"Answer as honestly as possible. The purpose is to understand your health, "
"not to judge you.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “I do not smoke.”\n"
"- “I drink occasionally.”\n"
"- “I exercise two or three times a week.”\n"
"- “I sit at a desk for most of the day.”\n"
"- “I have been sleeping less than usual.”\n"
"- “My work has been particularly stressful recently.”\n"
"- “There have been no major lifestyle changes.”\n"
"\n"
"## Ask the Doctor to Clarify\n"
"\n"
"Medical explanations may contain unfamiliar words. It is always acceptable "
"to ask for simpler language.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could you explain that in simpler terms?”\n"
"- “What does that word mean?”\n"
"- “Could you repeat that more slowly?”\n"
"- “Could you write the name down?”\n"
"- “I’m not sure I understood.”\n"
"- “Does that mean the problem is serious?”\n"
"- “Could you show me where that is?”\n"
"- “Could you explain what you are checking for?”\n"
"- “Could you give me the instructions in writing?”\n"
"\n"
"To check your understanding, summarize what you heard:\n"
"\n"
"> “So you are saying that we need more information before we know what is "
"causing the problem. Is that correct?”\n"
"\n"
"## Understand Examinations and Tests\n"
"\n"
"During a consultation, a doctor may suggest an examination or test to "
"gather more information.\n"
"\n"
"Common examples include:\n"
"\n"
"- A physical examination\n"
"- A blood test\n"
"- A urine test\n"
"- A swab\n"
"- An X-ray\n"
"- An ultrasound\n"
"- Another type of scan\n"
"- A referral to a specialist\n"
"- Monitoring the symptoms for a period of time\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “What is this test for?”\n"
"- “How should I prepare?”\n"
"- “Will it be painful?”\n"
"- “Are there any risks?”\n"
"- “How long will it take?”\n"
"- “When will the results be available?”\n"
"- “How will I receive the results?”\n"
"- “Do I need another appointment?”\n"
"- “What happens if the result is abnormal?”\n"
"- “Is there an alternative?”\n"
"\n"
"The AI roleplay should only help you practise these conversations. It "
"should not claim that a particular test is medically necessary for your "
"real symptoms.\n"
"\n"
"## Discuss a Possible Plan\n"
"\n"
"A real doctor may explain possible next steps, but you should ask questions "
"before agreeing to anything you do not understand.\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “What are the next steps?”\n"
"- “What are the available options?”\n"
"- “What is the purpose of this medication?”\n"
"- “How should it be taken?”\n"
"- “Are there common side effects?”\n"
"- “Could it interact with my other medication?”\n"
"- “How soon should I expect an improvement?”\n"
"- “What should I do if it does not help?”\n"
"- “Is there anything I should avoid?”\n"
"- “Do I need to change my normal activities?”\n"
"\n"
"You can also ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Are there any alternatives?”\n"
"- “What would happen if we waited?”\n"
"- “Do I need to decide today?”\n"
"- “Could I have some written information?”\n"
"- “Should I speak with a specialist?”\n"
"\n"
"The roleplay may practise asking these questions, but it must not prescribe "
"medication or create a real treatment plan.\n"
"\n"
"## Confirm Medication Instructions\n"
"\n"
"If a real clinician prescribes medication, confirm exactly how it should be "
"used.\n"
"\n"
"You may need to understand:\n"
"\n"
"- The medication name\n"
"- The dose\n"
"- How often to take it\n"
"- When to take it\n"
"- How long to take it\n"
"- Whether to take it with food\n"
"- Possible side effects\n"
"- What to do if you miss a dose\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “How often should I take it?”\n"
"- “Should I take it before or after food?”\n"
"- “How many days should I use it?”\n"
"- “What should I do if I miss a dose?”\n"
"- “Are there any side effects I should watch for?”\n"
"- “Can I take it with my other medication?”\n"
"- “Could you write the instructions down?”\n"
"\n"
"Do not rely on the roleplay for real dosing instructions. Follow the "
"directions given by your doctor or pharmacist.\n"
"\n"
"## Ask When to Seek More Help\n"
"\n"
"Before leaving, ask what to do if the symptoms continue or become worse.\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “When should I contact the clinic again?”\n"
"- “What should I do if the symptoms get worse?”\n"
"- “Which changes should I watch for?”\n"
"- “When should I arrange a follow-up?”\n"
"- “Who should I contact outside normal hours?”\n"
"- “Should I go to urgent care if this happens again?”\n"
"- “How long should I wait before asking for another appointment?”\n"
"\n"
"A real healthcare professional can give safety instructions based on your "
"specific situation. A simulation cannot assess your personal medical risk.\n"
"\n"
"## Request a Referral or Follow-Up\n"
"\n"
"The doctor may recommend another appointment or referral.\n"
"\n"
"You can ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Do I need to see a specialist?”\n"
"- “Will you send the referral?”\n"
"- “Do I need to contact the specialist myself?”\n"
"- “How long does the referral usually take?”\n"
"- “Should I book a follow-up appointment?”\n"
"- “When should I come back?”\n"
"- “Will we discuss the test results at the next visit?”\n"
"- “Can the follow-up be done by phone?”\n"
"\n"
"Before leaving, confirm who is responsible for the next action.\n"
"\n"
"## Discuss Privacy or Sensitive Topics\n"
"\n"
"Some health concerns may be difficult to discuss.\n"
"\n"
"You can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “This is difficult for me to talk about.”\n"
"- “I would prefer to discuss this privately.”\n"
"- “Could the other person leave the room?”\n"
"- “Could I speak with a doctor of a particular gender?”\n"
"- “I need a moment before I continue.”\n"
"- “I’m not sure how to describe the problem.”\n"
"- “Could I write it down instead?”\n"
"\n"
"You can also ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Will this information remain confidential?”\n"
"- “Who will have access to my medical information?”\n"
"- “Can I bring someone I trust into the consultation?”\n"
"\n"
"## Take Notes and Check Your Understanding\n"
"\n"
"It can be difficult to remember everything discussed during an appointment.\n"
"\n"
"You can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “Do you mind if I take notes?”\n"
"- “Could you write down the important instructions?”\n"
"- “Could you repeat the name of the test?”\n"
"- “Can I receive a summary after the appointment?”\n"
"- “Let me make sure I understood correctly.”\n"
"\n"
"A useful method is to repeat the plan in your own words:\n"
"\n"
"> “So I need to complete the test, continue tracking the symptoms, and "
"arrange another appointment after the results are available. Is that "
"correct?”\n"
"\n"
"This technique helps identify misunderstandings before you leave.\n"
"\n"
"## A Simple Doctor Conversation\n"
"\n"
"A typical consultation may look like this:\n"
"\n"
"> **Doctor:** What brings you in today?  \n"
"> **Patient:** I’ve had pain in my lower back for about a week, and it is "
"not improving.  \n"
"> **Doctor:** Did it begin suddenly or gradually?  \n"
"> **Patient:** Gradually. I first noticed it after working at my desk for "
"several hours.  \n"
"> **Doctor:** How would you describe the pain?  \n"
"> **Patient:** It is usually a dull ache, but I sometimes feel a sharp pain "
"when I stand up.  \n"
"> **Doctor:** How severe is it?  \n"
"> **Patient:** About five out of ten. It is worse in the evening.  \n"
"> **Doctor:** Have you tried anything for it?  \n"
"> **Patient:** I have been resting, but that has not made much difference.  "
"\n"
"> **Doctor:** Do you have any other symptoms?  \n"
"> **Patient:** No, I have not noticed anything else.  \n"
"> **Doctor:** Thank you. I would now ask some additional questions and "
"explain what a clinician might examine.  \n"
"> **Patient:** Before we continue, could you explain what you are checking "
"for?\n"
"\n"
"## A Simple Symptom Formula\n"
"\n"
"When describing a health concern, include:\n"
"\n"
"1. **Main symptom:** What is bothering you?\n"
"2. **Location:** Where do you feel it?\n"
"3. **Onset:** When and how did it begin?\n"
"4. **Description:** What does it feel like?\n"
"5. **Severity:** How strong or disruptive is it?\n"
"6. **Pattern:** Is it constant, occasional, improving, or worsening?\n"
"7. **Triggers:** What makes it better or worse?\n"
"8. **Other symptoms:** Have you noticed anything else?\n"
"9. **Previous attempts:** What have you already tried?\n"
"10. **Questions:** What do you want the doctor to explain?\n"
"\n"
"For example:\n"
"\n"
"> “I’ve had a sharp pain in my right shoulder for ten days. It is about six "
"out of ten and becomes worse when I lift my arm. Rest helps a little, but "
"the problem is not improving.”\n"
"\n"
"## Practice Scenario\n"
"\n"
"In this roleplay, you are attending an appointment with Dr. Ash. The AI "
"doctor will help you practise describing a health concern, answering common "
"questions, and understanding the structure of a medical consultation.\n"
"\n"
"During the conversation, try to:\n"
"\n"
"- Give a short summary of your main concern.\n"
"- Explain when the symptoms started.\n"
"- Describe their location, severity, and frequency.\n"
"- Say what makes them better or worse.\n"
"- Mention any related symptoms.\n"
"- Explain what you have already tried.\n"
"- Answer general questions about medication, allergies, and medical "
"history.\n"
"- Ask for clarification when you do not understand something.\n"
"- Ask what a real patient might need to confirm about tests or next steps.\n"
"- Summarize the conversation in your own words before it ends.\n"
"\n"
"Focus on describing your experience clearly. Do not use this simulation to "
"obtain a diagnosis, medication recommendation, or treatment plan."
msgstr ""
"Bercakap dengan doktor boleh menjadi sukar, terutama apabila anda perlu "
"menerangkan gejala dalam bahasa lain. Anda mungkin perlu menjelaskan apa "
"yang anda rasa, bila masalah bermula, betapa seriusnya, dan bagaimana ia "
"mempengaruhi kehidupan harian anda.\n"
"\n"
"Anda tidak memerlukan kosa kata perubatan lanjutan. Penerangan jelas, "
"contoh khusus, dan jawapan jujur biasanya lebih berguna daripada cuba "
"meneka nama keadaan.\n"
"\n"
"Peranan ini hanya untuk latihan bahasa. Ia tidak dapat mendiagnosis keadaan "
"perubatan, mengesyorkan rawatan, atau menggantikan penjagaan perubatan "
"profesional. Jika anda percaya anda mungkin mengalami kecemasan perubatan, "
"hubungi perkhidmatan kecemasan tempatan anda.\n"
"\n"
"## Mulakan Konsultasi\n"
"\n"
"Seorang doktor mungkin mula dengan bertanya:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Apa yang membawa anda ke sini hari ini?\"\n"
"- \"Bagaimana saya boleh membantu anda?\"\n"
"- \"Apa yang nampaknya menjadi masalah?\"\n"
"- \"Boleh anda menerangkan gejala anda?\"\n"
"- \"Bila ini bermula?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda pernah mengalami ini sebelum ini?\"\n"
"\n"
"Anda boleh mula dengan ringkasan pendek:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Saya mengalami batuk berterusan selama kira-kira seminggu.\"\n"
"- \"Saya mengalami kesakitan di bahagian bawah belakang saya.\"\n"
"- \"Saya berasa tidak bermaya baru-baru ini.\"\n"
"- \"Saya mempunyai ruam pada lengan saya yang tidak semakin baik.\"\n"
"- \"Saya sering mengalami sakit kepala berbanding biasa.\"\n"
"- \"Saya di sini untuk membincangkan keputusan ujian baru-baru ini.\"\n"
"- \"Saya sedang mengikuti masalah yang kita bincangkan sebelum ini.\"\n"
"\n"
"Struktur pembukaan yang berguna adalah:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Saya mengalami [gejala] untuk [jangka masa], dan ia [berkurang, semakin "
"teruk, atau tetap sama].\"\n"
"\n"
"Sebagai contoh:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Saya mengalami sakit di bahu kanan saya selama kira-kira sepuluh hari, "
"dan ia nampaknya semakin teruk.\"\n"
"\n"
"## Terangkan Di Mana Masalahnya\n"
"\n"
"Jadilah spesifik sebanyak mungkin tentang lokasi kesakitan atau "
"ketidakselesaan.\n"
"\n"
"Frasa yang berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Kesakitan berada di bahagian bawah belakang saya.\"\n"
"- \"Ia sakit di sebelah kanan dada saya.\"\n"
"- \"Saya merasa tidak selesa di belakang lutut kiri saya.\"\n"
"- \"Kesakitan bermula di leher saya dan bergerak ke bahu saya.\"\n"
"- \"Ruam terutama berada di lengan saya.\"\n"
"- \"Seluruh badan saya berasa sakit.\"\n"
"- \"Sukar untuk mengenal pasti lokasi yang tepat.\"\n"
"- \"Kesakitan nampaknya bergerak.\"\n"
"\n"
"Doktor mungkin bertanya:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Bolehkah anda menunjukkan di mana yang sakit?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah ia di satu sisi atau kedua-dua sisi?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah kesakitan bergerak ke tempat lain?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah ketidakselesaan itu dekat dengan permukaan atau lebih dalam?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah kawasan yang terjejas sensitif untuk disentuh?\"\n"
"\n"
"## Terangkan Bila Ia Bermula\n"
"\n"
"Doktor sering bertanya bila gejala bermula dan adakah ada sesuatu yang "
"berlaku sebelum itu.\n"
"\n"
"Anda boleh berkata:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Ia bermula pagi ini.\"\n"
"- \"Saya mula perasan tiga hari lalu.\"\n"
"- \"Gejala bermula secara beransur-ansur.\"\n"
"- \"Ia bermula secara tiba-tiba semasa saya bersenam.\"\n"
"- \"Ia bermula setelah saya pulang dari perjalanan.\"\n"
"- \"Saya perasankannya selepas mula mengambil ubat baru.\"\n"
"- \"Saya terbangun dengan kesakitan.\"\n"
"- \"Saya tidak ingat dengan tepat bila ia bermula.\"\n"
"\n"
"Soalan-soalan berguna yang mungkin anda dengar:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Adakah ia bermula secara tiba-tiba atau beransur-ansur?\"\n"
"- \"Apa yang anda lakukan ketika ia bermula?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah ada yang luar biasa berlaku sebelum itu?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah gejala berubah sejak itu?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah terdapat kecederaan?\"\n"
"\n"
"## Terangkan Bagaimana Rasanya\n"
"\n"
"Cuba terangkan sensasi dan bukan hanya berkata sesuatu itu sakit.\n"
"\n"
"Kesakitan atau ketidakselesaan mungkin dirasai:\n"
"\n"
"- Tajam\n"
"- Tumpul\n"
"- Panas\n"
"- Berdenyut\n"
"- Menikam\n"
"- Sakit\n"
"- Kekejangan\n"
"- Ketat\n"
"- Berat\n"
"- Kesemutan\n"
"- Kebas\n"
"- Gatal\n"
"- Sensitif\n"
"- Lembut\n"
"\n"
"Contoh:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Ia berasa seperti sakit yang tumpul.\"\n"
"- \"Kadang-kadang saya terasa sakit yang tajam.\"\n"
"- \"Terdapat sensasi panas.\"\n"
"- \"Jari-jari saya berasa kebas.\"\n"
"- \"Kawasan ini gatal dan sensitif.\"\n"
"- \"Ia berasa seperti tekanan daripada kesakitan.\"\n"
"- \"Dada saya berasa ketat.\"\n"
"- \"Saya ada kesemutan pada tangan saya.\"\n"
"\n"
"Jika anda tidak tahu perkataan yang tepat, terangkannya dengan cara lain:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Ia berasa seolah-olah ada yang menekan di kawasan itu.\"\n"
"\n"
"## Terangkan Betapa Parahnya\n"
"\n"
"Doktor mungkin meminta anda menilai kesakitan atau ketidakselesaan pada "
"skala dari sifar hingga sepuluh.\n"
"\n"
"- **Sifar** bermaksud tiada kesakitan.\n"
"- **Sepuluh** bermaksud kesakitan yang terburuk yang dapat anda bayangkan.\n"
"\n"
"Anda boleh berkata:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Kesakitannya kira-kira empat daripada sepuluh.\"\n"
"- \"Ia ringan kebanyakan masa.\"\n"
"- \"Ia menjadi parah pada waktu petang.\"\n"
"- \"Ia tidak selesa, tetapi saya masih boleh bekerja.\"\n"
"- \"Kesakitannya cukup kuat untuk membangunkan saya.\"\n"
"- \"Ia sukar berjalan kerana itu.\"\n"
"- \"Gejala mengganggu aktiviti harian saya.\"\n"
"\n"
"Ia juga membantu untuk menjelaskan apa yang anda boleh atau tidak boleh "
"lakukan:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Saya boleh berjalan, tetapi mendaki tangga menyakitkan.\"\n"
"- \"Saya tidak boleh menumpukan perhatian di tempat kerja.\"\n"
"- \"Saya mengalami kesukaran tidur.\"\n"
"- \"Saya boleh makan seperti biasa.\"\n"
"- \"Saya menjadi penat selepas aktiviti fizikal kecil.\"\n"
"- \"Saya terpaksa berhenti bersenam.\"\n"
"\n"
"## Terangkan Seberapa Sering Ia Berlaku\n"
"\n"
"Gejala mungkin sentiasa ada atau datang dan pergi.\n"
"\n"
"Frasa-frasa berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Kesakitan adalah konsisten.\"\n"
"- \"Ia datang dan pergi.\"\n"
"- \"Ia berlaku beberapa kali sehari.\"\n"
"- \"Ia biasanya berlangsung sekitar dua puluh minit.\"\n"
"- \"Gejala lebih teruk di waktu pagi.\"\n"
"- \"Ia berlaku terutama selepas makan.\"\n"
"- \"Ia hanya berlaku apabila saya bersenam.\"\n"
"- \"Saya berasa lebih baik selepas berehat.\"\n"
"- \"Sepertinya tiada corak.\"\n"
"\n"
"Doktor mungkin bertanya:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Berapa lama setiap episod berlangsung?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah ia berlaku setiap hari?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah ia lebih teruk pada masa tertentu?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah ada yang mencetuskannya?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah ada yang membuatnya lebih baik?\"\n"
"\n"
"## Terangkan Apa yang Membuatnya Lebih Baik atau Lebih Buruk\n"
"\n"
"Terangkan sama ada pergerakan, makanan, rehat, ubat, atau faktor lain "
"mengubah gejala anda.\n"
"\n"
"Anda boleh berkata:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Ia menjadi lebih teruk apabila saya bergerak.\"\n"
"- \"Kesakitan meningkat apabila saya mengambil nafas dalam.\"\n"
"- \"Ia berasa lebih baik selepas saya berehat.\"\n"
"- \"Haba nampaknya membantu.\"\n"
"- \"Gejala lebih teruk selepas makan.\"\n"
"- \"Ia bertambah baik apabila saya berbaring.\"\n"
"- \"Penahan sakit membantu sementara.\"\n"
"- \"Tiada apa yang kelihatan membuat perbezaan.\"\n"
"- \"Masalah menjadi lebih teruk apabila saya tertekan.\"\n"
"\n"
"Kosakata yang berguna:\n"
"\n"
"- **Pencetus** — sesuatu yang menyebabkan atau memburukkan gejala\n"
"- **Melegakan** — membuat gejala kurang teruk\n"
"- **Menggoyahkan** — membuat gejala lebih teruk\n"
"\n"
"## Sebutkan Gejala Lain\n"
"\n"
"Doktor mungkin bertanya jika anda perasan sebarang perubahan lain.\n"
"\n"
"Soalan biasa termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda demam?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda merasa sakit atau muntah?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda perasan sebarang bengkak?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda hilang selera makan?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda mengalami pening?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda sesak nafas?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda mengalami kesukaran tidur?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda perasan sebarang perubahan berat badan anda?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda mengalami kelemahan atau kebas?\"\n"
"\n"
"Anda boleh menjawab:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Saya juga ada demam ringan.\"\n"
"- \"Saya merasa pening beberapa kali.\"\n"
"- \"Terdapat sedikit bengkak sekitar kawasan itu.\"\n"
"- \"Saya tidak perasan sebarang gejala lain.\"\n"
"- \"Selera makan saya adalah normal.\"\n"
"- \"Saya tidur dengan buruk.\"\n"
"- \"Saya rasa penat, tetapi saya tidak ada demam.\"\n"
"\n"
"Jangan tinggalkan simptom kerana anda fikir tidak berkaitan. Doktor boleh "
"memutuskan sama ada ia berkaitan.\n"
"\n"
"## Terangkan Apa yang Sudah Anda Cuba\n"
"\n"
"Beritahu doktor sama ada anda telah mengambil ubat, menukar rutin anda, "
"atau mencuba penyelesaian lain.\n"
"\n"
"Anda boleh berkata:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Saya telah berehat.\"\n"
"- \"Saya cuba penahan sakit yang boleh dibeli di kedai.\"\n"
"- \"Saya menggunakan kompres sejuk.\"\n"
"- \"Saya berhenti bersenam selama beberapa hari.\"\n"
"- \"Saya menukar diet saya, tetapi ia tidak membantu.\"\n"
"- \"Ubat itu membantu selama beberapa jam.\"\n"
"- \"Saya belum mencuba apa-apa lagi.\"\n"
"- \"Saya bercakap dengan ahli farmasi sebelum membuat temujanji ini.\"\n"
"\n"
"Bersedia untuk menjelaskan:\n"
"\n"
"- Apa yang anda gunakan\n"
"- Berapa banyak yang anda gunakan\n"
"- Berapa kerap anda gunakan\n"
"- Sama ada ia membantu\n"
"- Sama ada anda perasan kesan sampingan\n"
"\n"
"Jangan berpura-pura untuk mengingati butiran yang anda tidak tahu. Anda "
"boleh berkata:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Saya tidak ingat nama yang tepat.\"\n"
"- \"Saya boleh tunjukkan paketnya.\"\n"
"- \"Saya tidak pasti tentang dosanya.\"\n"
"- \"Saya mengambilnya mengikut arahan pada label.\"\n"
"\n"
"## Bincangkan Ubat Semasa\n"
"\n"
"Doktor mungkin mahu tahu tentang semua ubat dan suplemen yang anda ambil.\n"
"\n"
"Anda boleh berkata:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Saya mengambil ubat ini setiap pagi.\"\n"
"- \"Saya menggunakan penyedutan apabila diperlukan.\"\n"
"- \"Saya baru mula mengambil preskripsi baru.\"\n"
"- \"Saya berhenti mengambilnya minggu lepas.\"\n"
"- \"Sesekali saya mengambil penahan sakit yang boleh dibeli di kaunter.\"\n"
"- \"Saya tidak mengambil sebarang ubat pada masa ini.\"\n"
"- \"Saya ada senarai ubat-ubatan saya bersama saya.\"\n"
"\n"
"Doktor mungkin bertanya:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Apa dos yang anda ambil?\"\n"
"- \"Berapa lama anda telah mengambilnya?\"\n"
"- \"Siapa yang menetapkannya?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda telah ketinggalan sebarang dos?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda perasan sebarang kesan sampingan?\"\n"
"\n"
"Jangan berhenti ubat yang ditetapkan berdasarkan simulasi pembelajaran "
"bahasa sahaja. Bincangkan perubahan ubat dengan profesional penjagaan "
"kesihatan yang berkelayakan.\n"
"\n"
"## Sebutkan Alergi\n"
"\n"
"Beritahu doktor tentang ubat, makanan, atau alahan lain.\n"
"\n"
"Frasa berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Saya alergi terhadap penisilin.\"\n"
"- \"Saya ada alahan kacang yang teruk.\"\n"
"- \"Ubat ini menyebabkan ruam pada masa lalu.\"\n"
"- \"Saya tidak ada alahan yang diketahui.\"\n"
"- \"Saya tidak pasti sama ada ia adalah tindak balas alahan.\"\n"
"- \"Saya mengalami bengkak selepas mengambil ubat itu.\"\n"
"\n"
"Doktor mungkin bertanya apa yang berlaku semasa reaksi dan betapa seriusnya "
"ia.\n"
"\n"
"## Bincangkan Sejarah Perubatan Anda\n"
"\n"
"Doktor mungkin bertanya tentang penyakit sebelum ini, kecederaan, operasi, "
"atau gejala yang serupa.\n"
"\n"
"Anda boleh berkata:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Saya mengalami masalah yang sama dua tahun lalu.\"\n"
"- \"Saya mempunyai sejarah masalah belakang.\"\n"
"- \"Saya menjalani pembedahan lima tahun lalu.\"\n"
"- \"Saya telah dirawat untuk ini sebelum ini.\"\n"
"- \"Saya tidak pernah mengalami ini sebelum ini.\"\n"
"- \"Saya ada keadaan perubatan jangka panjang.\"\n"
"- \"Saya baru-baru ini di hospital.\"\n"
"- \"Saya telah membawa keputusan ujian saya sebelumnya.\"\n"
"\n"
"Anda juga mungkin ditanya tentang keadaan kesihatan dalam keluarga anda:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Adakah sesiapa dalam keluarga anda mempunyai keadaan yang serupa?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah terdapat sejarah keluarga penyakit jantung?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah mana-mana saudara terdekat mempunyai diabetes?\"\n"
"\n"
"Anda boleh berkata:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Bapa saya mempunyai keadaan yang serupa.\"\n"
"- \"Tiada sejarah keluarga yang diketahui.\"\n"
"- \"Saya tidak pasti.\"\n"
"- \"Saya perlu memeriksa.\"\n"
"\n"
"## Jawab Soalan Gaya Hidup\n"
"\n"
"Doktor mungkin bertanya tentang tidur, senaman, diet, alkohol, merokok, "
"kerja, atau tekanan kerana faktor-faktor ini boleh mempengaruhi kesihatan.\n"
"\n"
"Anda mungkin mendengar:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda merokok?\"\n"
"- \"Berapa kerap anda bersenam?\"\n"
"- \"Berapa banyak alkohol yang anda minum?\"\n"
"- \"Bagaimana kualiti tidur anda?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah apa-apa yang berubah dalam diet anda?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda mengalami stres yang tidak biasa?\"\n"
"- \"Apa jenis kerja anda?\"\n"
"\n"
"Jawab sejujur mungkin. Tujuannya adalah untuk memahami kesihatan anda, "
"bukan untuk menilai anda.\n"
"\n"
"Frasa berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Saya tidak merokok.\"\n"
"- \"Saya minum sesekali.\"\n"
"- \"Saya bersenam dua atau tiga kali seminggu.\"\n"
"- \"Saya duduk di meja kebanyakan hari.\"\n"
"- \"Saya tidur kurang daripada biasa.\"\n"
"- \"Kerja saya sangat menekan baru-baru ini.\"\n"
"- \"Tiada perubahan besar dalam gaya hidup.\"\n"
"\n"
"## Minta Penjelasan Doktor\n"
"\n"
"Penjelasan perubatan mungkin mengandungi perkataan yang tidak biasa. Ia "
"selalu boleh diterima untuk meminta bahasa yang lebih mudah.\n"
"\n"
"Frasa berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Boleh anda jelaskan dalam istilah yang lebih mudah?\"\n"
"- \"Apa maksud perkataan itu?\"\n"
"- \"Boleh anda ulangi lebih perlahan?\"\n"
"- \"Boleh anda tulis nama itu?\"\n"
"- \"Saya tidak pasti saya faham.\"\n"
"- \"Adakah itu bermaksud masalah ini serius?\"\n"
"- \"Boleh anda tunjukkan di mana ia?\"\n"
"- \"Boleh anda jelaskan apa yang anda periksa?\"\n"
"- \"Boleh anda beri saya arahan secara bertulis?\"\n"
"\n"
"Untuk memeriksa pemahaman anda, ringkaskan apa yang anda dengar:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Jadi anda berkata bahawa kita perlukan lebih banyak maklumat sebelum "
"kita tahu apa yang menyebabkan masalah. Adakah itu betul?\"\n"
"\n"
"## Fahami Pemeriksaan dan Ujian\n"
"\n"
"Semasa konsultasi, seorang doktor mungkin mencadangkan pemeriksaan atau "
"ujian untuk mendapatkan lebih banyak maklumat.\n"
"\n"
"Contoh umum termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- Pemeriksaan fizikal\n"
"- Ujian darah\n"
"- Ujian air kencing\n"
"- Swab\n"
"- X-ray\n"
"- Ultrasound\n"
"- Jenis pengimbasan lain\n"
"- Rujukan kepada pakar\n"
"- Memantau gejala untuk tempoh tertentu\n"
"\n"
"Soalan berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Apa tujuan ujian ini?\"\n"
"- \"Bagaimana saya perlu bersedia?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah ia akan menyakitkan?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah terdapat risiko?\"\n"
"- \"Berapa lama ia akan mengambil?\"\n"
"- \"Bilakah keputusan akan tersedia?\"\n"
"- \"Bagaimana saya akan menerima keputusan?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah saya memerlukan temujanji lain?\"\n"
"- \"Apa yang berlaku jika keputusan itu tidak normal?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah terdapat alternatif?\"\n"
"\n"
"Peranan AI ini harus hanya membantu anda berlatih perbualan ini. Ia tidak "
"boleh mengaku bahawa ujian tertentu diperlukan secara perubatan untuk "
"gejala sebenar anda.\n"
"\n"
"## Bincangkan Rancangan yang Mungkin\n"
"\n"
"Seorang doktor sebenar mungkin menerangkan langkah seterusnya yang mungkin, "
"tetapi anda harus bertanya soalan sebelum bersetuju dengan apa-apa yang "
"anda tidak faham.\n"
"\n"
"Soalan berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Apa langkah seterusnya?\"\n"
"- \"Apa pilihan yang ada?\"\n"
"- \"Apa tujuan ubat ini?\"\n"
"- \"Bagaimana ia harus diambil?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah kesan sampingan yang biasa?\"\n"
"- \"Bolehkah ia berinteraksi dengan ubat lain saya?\"\n"
"- \"Berapa cepat saya boleh mengharapkan perubahan?\"\n"
"- \"Apa yang perlu saya lakukan jika ia tidak membantu?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah apa-apa yang perlu saya elakkan?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah saya perlu menukar aktiviti biasa saya?\"\n"
"\n"
"Anda juga boleh bertanya:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Adakah terdapat sebarang alternatif?\"\n"
"- \"Apa yang akan berlaku jika kita menunggu?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah saya perlu membuat keputusan hari ini?\"\n"
"- \"Bolehkah saya mendapat sedikit maklumat bertulis?\"\n"
"- \"Perlukah saya berbicara dengan pakar?\"\n"
"\n"
"Peranan ini mungkin berlatih menanyakan soalan ini, tetapi ia tidak harus "
"menetapkan ubat atau membuat rancangan rawatan sebenar.\n"
"\n"
"## Sahkan Arahan Ubat\n"
"\n"
"Jika seorang klinis sebenar menetapkan ubat, sahkan dengan tepat bagaimana "
"ia harus digunakan.\n"
"\n"
"Anda mungkin perlu memahami:\n"
"\n"
"- Nama ubat\n"
"- Dos\n"
"- Berapa kerap untuk mengambilnya\n"
"- Bila untuk mengambilnya\n"
"- Berapa lama untuk mengambilnya\n"
"- Sama ada untuk mengambilnya dengan makanan\n"
"- Kesan sampingan yang mungkin\n"
"- Apa yang perlu dilakukan jika terlepas dos\n"
"\n"
"Frasa berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Berapa kerap saya harus mengambilnya?\"\n"
"- \"Perlukah saya mengambilnya sebelum atau selepas makanan?\"\n"
"- \"Berapa hari saya harus menggunakannya?\"\n"
"- \"Apa yang perlu saya buat jika saya terlepas dos?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah terdapat kesan sampingan yang perlu saya ambil perhatian?\"\n"
"- \"Bolehkah saya mengambilnya dengan ubat lain saya?\"\n"
"- \"Boleh anda tuliskan arahan?\"\n"
"\n"
"Jangan bergantung kepada peranan ini untuk arahan dos sebenar. Ikut arahan "
"yang diberikan oleh doktor atau ahli farmasi anda.\n"
"\n"
"## Tanya Bila Perlu Mencari Lebih Banyak Bantuan\n"
"\n"
"Sebelum meninggalkan, tanyakan apa yang perlu dilakukan jika gejalanya "
"berlanjutan atau menjadi lebih buruk.\n"
"\n"
"Soalan berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Bila saya harus menghubungi klinik lagi?\"\n"
"- \"Apa yang perlu saya buat jika gejala menjadi lebih buruk?\"\n"
"- \"Perubahan apa yang perlu saya ambil perhatian?\"\n"
"- \"Bila saya harus mengatur susulan?\"\n"
"- \"Siapa yang perlu saya hubungi di luar waktu biasa?\"\n"
"- \"Patutkah saya pergi ke rawatan kecemasan jika ini berlaku lagi?\"\n"
"- \"Berapa lama saya perlu tunggu sebelum meminta temujanji lain?\"\n"
"\n"
"Seorang profesional penjagaan kesihatan sebenar boleh memberikan arahan "
"keselamatan berdasarkan situasi khusus anda. Simulasi tidak dapat menilai "
"risiko perubatan peribadi anda. \n"
"\n"
"## Minta Rujukan atau Susulan\n"
"\n"
"Doktor mungkin mengesyorkan temujanji lain atau rujukan.\n"
"\n"
"Anda boleh bertanya:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Adakah saya perlu berjumpa pakar?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah anda akan menghantar rujukan?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah saya perlu menghubungi pakar itu sendiri?\"\n"
"- \"Berapa lama biasanya rujukan mengambil?\"\n"
"- \"Saya perlu membuat temujanji susulan?\"\n"
"- \"Bila saya harus kembali?\"\n"
"- \"Adakah kita akan membincangkan keputusan ujian pada lawatan "
"berikutnya?\"\n"
"- \"Bolehkah susulan dilakukan melalui telefon?\"\n"
"\n"
"Sebelum meninggalkan, pastikan siapa yang bertanggungjawab untuk tindakan "
"seterusnya.\n"
"\n"
"## Bincangkan Privasi atau Topik Sensitif\n"
"\n"
"Beberapa kebimbangan kesihatan mungkin sukar untuk dibincangkan.\n"
"\n"
"Anda boleh berkata:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Sukar bagi saya untuk bercakap tentang ini.\"\n"
"- \"Saya lebih suka membincangkan ini secara peribadi.\"\n"
"- \"Boleh orang lain keluar dari bilik?\"\n"
"- \"Boleh saya bercakap dengan doktor dengan jantina tertentu?\"\n"
"- \"Saya perlukan sekejap sebelum saya meneruskan.\"\n"
"- \"Saya tidak pasti bagaimana untuk menggambarkan masalah ini.\"\n"
"- \"Bolehkah saya tuliskannya sebagai gantinya?\"\n"
"\n"
"Anda juga boleh bertanya:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Adakah maklumat ini akan kekal sulit?\"\n"
"- \"Siapa yang akan mempunyai akses kepada maklumat perubatan saya?\"\n"
"- \"Bolehkah saya membawa seseorang yang saya percayai ke dalam "
"konsultasi?\"\n"
"\n"
"## Ambil Nota dan Periksa Pemahaman Anda\n"
"\n"
"Boleh jadi sukar untuk mengingati segala-galanya yang dibincangkan semasa "
"temujanji.\n"
"\n"
"Anda boleh berkata:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Adakah ia mengganggu jika saya mengambil nota?\"\n"
"- \"Boleh anda menuliskan arahan penting?\"\n"
"- \"Boleh anda ulangi nama ujian itu?\"\n"
"- \"Bolehkah saya menerima ringkasan selepas temujanji?\"\n"
"- \"Biar saya pastikan saya faham dengan betul.\"\n"
"\n"
"Kaedah yang berguna adalah untuk mengulangi rancangan dalam kata-kata anda "
"sendiri:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Jadi saya perlu melengkapkan ujian itu, terus memantau gejala, dan "
"mengatur temujanji lain selepas keputusan tersedia. Adakah itu betul?\"\n"
"\n"
"Teknik ini membantu mengenal pasti salah faham sebelum anda pergi.\n"
"\n"
"## Perbualan Doktor yang Mudah\n"
"\n"
"Konsultasi tipikal mungkin kelihatan seperti ini:\n"
"\n"
"> **Doktor:** Apa yang membawa anda ke sini hari ini?  \n"
"> **Pesakit:** Saya mengalami kesakitan di bahagian bawah belakang saya "
"selama kira-kira seminggu, dan ia tidak bertambah baik.  \n"
"> **Doktor:** Adakah ia bermula secara tiba-tiba atau beransur-ansur?  \n"
"> **Pesakit:** Secara beransur-ansur. Saya mula perasan selepas bekerja di "
"meja selama beberapa jam.  \n"
"> **Doktor:** Bagaimana anda menggambarkan kesakitan?  \n"
"> **Pesakit:** Ia biasanya sakit yang tumpul, tetapi saya kadang-kadang "
"merasa sakit yang tajam apabila saya bangun berdiri.  \n"
"> **Doktor:** Seberapa parahkah ia?  \n"
"> **Pesakit:** Kira-kira lima dari sepuluh. Ia lebih teruk pada waktu "
"petang.  \n"
"> **Doktor:** Adakah anda mencuba apa-apa untuk ini?  \n"
"> **Pesakit:** Saya berehat, tetapi itu tidak banyak membuat perbezaan.  \n"
"> **Doktor:** Adakah anda mempunyai simptom lain?  \n"
"> **Pesakit:** Tidak, saya tidak perasan yang lain.   \n"
"> **Doktor:** Terima kasih. Saya akan bertanya beberapa soalan tambahan dan "
"menjelaskan apa yang mungkin diperiksa oleh klinis.   \n"
"> **Pesakit:** Sebelum kita teruskan, boleh anda jelaskan apa yang anda "
"periksa?\n"
"\n"
"## Formula Simptom Mudah\n"
"\n"
"Apabila menerangkan kebimbangan kesihatan, sertakan:\n"
"\n"
"1. **Gejala Utama:** Apa yang mengganggu anda?\n"
"2. **Lokasi:** Di mana anda merasakannya?\n"
"3. **Permulaan:** Bila dan bagaimana ia bermula?\n"
"4. **Penerangan:** Apa rasanya?\n"
"5. **Severiti:** Seberapa kuat atau mengganggu ia?\n"
"6. **Pola:** Adakah ia tetap, sesekali, bertambah baik, atau semakin teruk?\n"
"7. **Pencetus:** Apa yang membuatnya lebih baik atau lebih buruk?\n"
"8. **Gejala Lain:** Adakah anda perasan yang lain?\n"
"9. **Percubaan Sebelumnya:** Apa yang sudah anda cuba?\n"
"10. **Soalan:** Apa yang anda ingin doktor jelaskan?\n"
"\n"
"Sebagai contoh:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Saya mengalami sakit tajam di bahu kanan saya selama sepuluh hari. Ia "
"kira-kira enam dari sepuluh dan menjadi lebih buruk apabila saya mengangkat "
"tangan saya. Rehat membantu sedikit, tetapi masalah ini tidak bertambah "
"baik.\"\n"
"\n"
"## Latihan Senario\n"
"\n"
"Dalam peranan ini, anda menghadiri temujanji dengan Dr. Ash. Doktor AI akan "
"membantu anda berlatih menerangkan kebimbangan kesihatan, menjawab soalan "
"biasa, dan memahami struktur konsultasi perubatan.\n"
"\n"
"Semasa perbualan, cuba:\n"
"\n"
"- Berikan ringkasan pendek tentang kebimbangan utama anda.\n"
"- Terangkan bila gejala bermula.\n"
"- Terangkan lokasi, severiti, dan kekerapan mereka.\n"
"- Katakan apa yang membuat mereka lebih baik atau lebih buruk.\n"
"- Sebut sebarang gejala berkaitan.\n"
"- Terangkan apa yang sudah anda cuba.\n"
"- Jawab soalan umum tentang ubat, alahan, dan sejarah perubatan.\n"
"- Minta penjelasan apabila anda tidak faham sesuatu.\n"
"- Tanya apa yang mungkin perlu disahkan oleh pesakit sebenar tentang ujian "
"atau langkah seterusnya.\n"
"- Ringkaskan perbualan dalam kata-kata anda sendiri sebelum ia berakhir.\n"
"\n"
"Fokus pada menerangkan pengalaman anda dengan jelas. Jangan gunakan "
"simulasi ini untuk mendapatkan diagnosis, cadangan ubat, atau rancangan "
"rawatan."

#: src/features/RolePlay/scenarios/small-talk-with-a-stranger.ts:13
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid ""
"Talking to a stranger can feel uncomfortable because neither person knows "
"what to say yet. The goal is not to sound especially clever or interesting. "
"Your first goal is simply to make the other person feel comfortable and "
"discover something you can talk about together.\n"
"\n"
"The advice below is inspired by ideas from Charles Duhigg’s book "
"*Supercommunicators*.\n"
"\n"
"## How to Start a Conversation\n"
"\n"
"Use the situation you already share. You do not need an original or "
"impressive opening line.\n"
"\n"
"Try making a simple observation and adding an easy question:\n"
"\n"
"- “This place is busier than I expected. Have you been here before?”\n"
"- “How do you know the host?”\n"
"- “What brought you to this event?”\n"
"- “That looks interesting. What are you drinking?”\n"
"- “Is this your first time at an event like this?”\n"
"\n"
"Questions about the immediate situation feel natural because they give the "
"other person an obvious way to respond.\n"
"\n"
"## Ask Questions That Reveal More Than Facts\n"
"\n"
"Basic questions are useful for starting a conversation:\n"
"\n"
"- “Where are you from?”\n"
"- “What do you do?”\n"
"- “Do you live nearby?”\n"
"\n"
"However, a conversation becomes more interesting when you gently ask about "
"the person’s experiences, feelings, or preferences.\n"
"\n"
"Instead of only asking:\n"
"\n"
"> “What do you do for work?”\n"
"\n"
"You could continue with:\n"
"\n"
"> “What do you enjoy most about it?”\n"
"\n"
"Instead of:\n"
"\n"
"> “How long have you lived here?”\n"
"\n"
"Try:\n"
"\n"
"> “What do you like most about living here?”\n"
"\n"
"Other useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “How did you become interested in that?”\n"
"- “What has been the best part of your week?”\n"
"- “What do you usually enjoy doing on weekends?”\n"
"- “What is something you are looking forward to?”\n"
"- “What kind of places do you like visiting?”\n"
"\n"
"These questions are personal enough to create a connection, but still safe "
"and appropriate for someone you have just met.\n"
"\n"
"## Listen for the Kind of Conversation They Want\n"
"\n"
"People do not always want the same thing from a conversation. They may want "
"to:\n"
"\n"
"1. Exchange information or make a decision.\n"
"2. Share an emotion or experience.\n"
"3. Talk about their interests, identity, or relationships.\n"
"\n"
"Try to respond to the kind of conversation the other person has started.\n"
"\n"
"If someone says:\n"
"\n"
"> “I moved here two weeks ago and everything still feels unfamiliar.”\n"
"\n"
"A purely practical response might be:\n"
"\n"
"> “You should download a city guide.”\n"
"\n"
"But an emotional response may connect better:\n"
"\n"
"> “That sounds exciting, but probably a little overwhelming too. How has it "
"been so far?”\n"
"\n"
"You do not always need to solve a problem. Sometimes people simply want to "
"feel understood.\n"
"\n"
"## Show That You Are Really Listening\n"
"\n"
"A useful technique is to:\n"
"\n"
"1. Ask a question.\n"
"2. Listen carefully.\n"
"3. Summarize the important part in your own words.\n"
"4. Check whether you understood correctly.\n"
"\n"
"For example:\n"
"\n"
"> “So you started learning photography because you wanted a creative hobby "
"outside work. Did I understand that correctly?”\n"
"\n"
"You do not need to do this formally after every answer. Short natural "
"responses also work:\n"
"\n"
"- “So that is what brought you here.”\n"
"- “It sounds like you really enjoyed it.”\n"
"- “I can see why that was frustrating.”\n"
"- “So you prefer quieter places?”\n"
"- “That makes sense.”\n"
"\n"
"These responses show that you are not simply waiting for your turn to "
"speak.\n"
"\n"
"## Share Something About Yourself Too\n"
"\n"
"Good small talk should not feel like an interview. After asking a question, "
"share a related detail about yourself.\n"
"\n"
"For example:\n"
"\n"
"> “What kind of music do you listen to? I’ve been listening to a lot of "
"jazz recently, but I’m trying to discover something new.”\n"
"\n"
"Or:\n"
"\n"
"> “Have you travelled anywhere interesting recently? I visited a small town "
"by a lake last weekend and really enjoyed it.”\n"
"\n"
"A useful pattern is:\n"
"\n"
"**Ask → Listen → Respond → Share → Ask again**\n"
"\n"
"This creates a balanced conversation in which both people gradually reveal "
"more about themselves.\n"
"\n"
"## How to Keep the Conversation Going\n"
"\n"
"Listen for a detail you can explore.\n"
"\n"
"If the person says:\n"
"\n"
"> “I recently started running.”\n"
"\n"
"You could ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “What made you start?”\n"
"- “Do you prefer running alone or with other people?”\n"
"- “Was it difficult in the beginning?”\n"
"- “Are you training for anything?”\n"
"\n"
"You do not need to introduce a completely new topic after every answer. "
"Often, the easiest way to continue is to become curious about one detail "
"the person has already mentioned.\n"
"\n"
"## What to Avoid\n"
"\n"
"Try not to:\n"
"\n"
"- Ask many unrelated questions one after another.\n"
"- Turn every answer back to yourself.\n"
"- Give advice before understanding what the person needs.\n"
"- Ask questions that are too personal too quickly.\n"
"- Pretend to understand when you are confused.\n"
"- Focus so much on perfect grammar that you stop listening.\n"
"\n"
"It is completely natural to pause, search for a word, or ask someone to "
"repeat themselves.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Sorry, could you say that again?”\n"
"- “What do you mean by that?”\n"
"- “I’m not sure I understood correctly.”\n"
"- “How would you describe it?”\n"
"- “Give me a second—I’m trying to find the right word.”\n"
"\n"
"## How to End the Conversation Politely\n"
"\n"
"Not every conversation needs to last a long time. You can finish warmly "
"without making the moment awkward:\n"
"\n"
"- “It was really nice talking to you.”\n"
"- “I’m going to get another drink, but I’m glad we met.”\n"
"- “I’ll let you talk to the others, but I enjoyed our conversation.”\n"
"- “I hope you enjoy the rest of the event.”\n"
"- “Maybe I’ll see you again later.”\n"
"\n"
"Ending a conversation politely is also an important communication skill.\n"
"\n"
"## A Simple Conversation Formula\n"
"\n"
"When you are unsure what to do, remember:\n"
"\n"
"1. **Open:** Comment on the shared situation.\n"
"2. **Explore:** Ask about an experience, preference, or feeling.\n"
"3. **Listen:** Respond to something specific they said.\n"
"4. **Connect:** Share a related detail about yourself.\n"
"5. **Continue or close:** Ask a follow-up question or end politely.\n"
"\n"
"## Practice Scenario\n"
"\n"
"In this roleplay, you are meeting a friendly stranger at a social event. "
"Start with an easy question, listen for interesting details, and gradually "
"move from basic facts to experiences and interests.\n"
"\n"
"Try to practice at least three skills:\n"
"\n"
"- Ask one question about an experience or feeling.\n"
"- Refer to something the stranger said earlier.\n"
"- Share something related about yourself.\n"
"\n"
"Do not worry about creating a perfect conversation. Concentrate on being "
"curious, attentive, and easy to talk to."
msgstr ""
"Bercakap dengan orang yang tidak dikenali boleh berasa tidak selesa kerana "
"masing-masing belum tahu apa yang hendak dikatakan. Matlamatnya bukan untuk "
"kedengaran terlalu bijak atau menarik. Matlamat pertama anda adalah "
"semata-mata untuk membuat orang lain berasa selesa dan menemui sesuatu yang "
"boleh anda bincangkan bersama.\n"
"\n"
"Nasihat di bawah diilhamkan oleh idea daripada buku Charles Duhigg "
"*Supercommunicators*.\n"
"\n"
"## Cara Memulakan Perbualan\n"
"\n"
"Gunakan situasi yang sudah anda kongsi. Anda tidak perlu pembukaan yang "
"asli atau mengagumkan.\n"
"\n"
"Cuba buat pemerhatian ringkas dan tambahkan soalan mudah:\n"
"\n"
"- “Tempat ini lebih sibuk daripada yang saya jangkakan. Adakah anda pernah "
"ke sini sebelum ini?”\n"
"- “Bagaimana anda mengenali tuan rumah?”\n"
"- “Apa yang membawa anda ke acara ini?”\n"
"- “Itu kelihatan menarik. Apa yang anda minum?”\n"
"- “Adakah ini kali pertama anda di acara seperti ini?”\n"
"\n"
"Soalan tentang situasi semasa berasa semula jadi kerana ia memberi orang "
"lain cara yang jelas untuk memberi respons.\n"
"\n"
"## Tanya Soalan Yang Mendedahkan Lebih Daripada Fakta\n"
"\n"
"Soalan asas berguna untuk memulakan perbualan:\n"
"\n"
"- “Dari mana anda berasal?”\n"
"- “Apa yang anda lakukan?”\n"
"- “Adakah anda tinggal berdekatan?”\n"
"\n"
"Walau bagaimanapun, perbualan menjadi lebih menarik apabila anda dengan "
"lembut bertanya tentang pengalaman, perasaan, atau pilihan orang itu.\n"
"\n"
"Daripada hanya bertanya:\n"
"\n"
"> “Apa yang anda lakukan untuk bekerja?”\n"
"\n"
"Anda boleh meneruskan dengan:\n"
"\n"
"> “Apa yang paling anda nikmati tentangnya?”\n"
"\n"
"Daripada:\n"
"\n"
"> “Berapa lama anda tinggal di sini?”\n"
"\n"
"Cuba:\n"
"\n"
"> “Apa yang paling anda suka tentang tinggal di sini?”\n"
"\n"
"Soalan berguna lain termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- “Bagaimana anda menjadi berminat dalam hal itu?”\n"
"- “Apa bahagian terbaik dalam minggu anda?”\n"
"- “Apa yang biasanya anda nikmati melakukan pada hujung minggu?”\n"
"- “Apa yang anda nantikan?”\n"
"- “Apa jenis tempat yang anda suka lawati?”\n"
"\n"
"Soalan-soalan ini cukup peribadi untuk mencipta hubungan, tetapi masih "
"selamat dan sesuai untuk seseorang yang baru anda temui.\n"
"\n"
"## Dengar Untuk Jenis Perbualan Yang Mereka Mahukan\n"
"\n"
"Orang tidak selalu mahukan perkara yang sama dari perbualan. Mereka mungkin "
"mahu:\n"
"\n"
"1. Bertukar maklumat atau membuat keputusan.\n"
"2. Berkongsi emosi atau pengalaman.\n"
"3. Bercakap tentang minat, identiti, atau hubungan mereka.\n"
"\n"
"Cuba respons kepada jenis perbualan yang dimulakan oleh orang lain.\n"
"\n"
"Jika seseorang berkata:\n"
"\n"
"> “Saya berpindah ke sini dua minggu lalu dan semuanya masih terasa asing.”\n"
"\n"
"Respons yang semata-mata praktikal mungkin:\n"
"\n"
"> “Anda patut muat turun panduan bandar.”\n"
"\n"
"Tetapi respons emosional mungkin lebih berhubung:\n"
"\n"
"> “Itu kedengaran menarik, tetapi mungkin agak mengelirukan juga. Bagaimana "
"ia setakat ini?”\n"
"\n"
"Anda tidak selalu perlu menyelesaikan masalah. Kadang-kadang orang hanya "
"mahu berasa difahami.\n"
"\n"
"## Tunjukkan Bahawa Anda Benar-benar Mendengar\n"
"\n"
"Satu teknik berguna adalah untuk:\n"
"\n"
"1. Tanya soalan.\n"
"2. Dengar dengan teliti.\n"
"3. Rangkuman fakta penting dalam kata-kata anda sendiri.\n"
"4. Periksa sama ada anda faham dengan betul.\n"
"\n"
"Sebagai contoh:\n"
"\n"
"> “Jadi anda mula belajar fotografi kerana anda mahukan hobi kreatif di "
"luar kerja. Adakah saya faham dengan betul?”\n"
"\n"
"Anda tidak perlu melakukan ini secara formal selepas setiap jawapan. "
"Respons natural yang ringkas juga berkesan:\n"
"\n"
"- “Itu membawa anda ke sini.”\n"
"- “Kedengarannya anda benar-benar menikmatinya.\"\n"
"- “Saya faham kenapa itu mengecewakan.”\n"
"- “Jadi anda lebih suka tempat yang lebih tenang?”\n"
"- “Itu masuk akal.”\n"
"\n"
"Respons-respons ini menunjukkan bahawa anda tidak hanya menunggu giliran "
"anda untuk bercakap.\n"
"\n"
"## Kongsi Sesuatu Tentang Diri Anda Juga\n"
"\n"
"Perbualan ringan yang baik tidak seharusnya terasa seperti temuduga. "
"Selepas bertanya soalan, kongsi maklumat mengenai diri anda yang berkaitan.\n"
"\n"
"Sebagai contoh:\n"
"\n"
"> “Apa jenis muzik yang anda dengar? Saya sedang banyak mendengar jazz "
"baru-baru ini, tetapi saya cuba untuk menemui sesuatu yang baru.”\n"
"\n"
"Atau:\n"
"\n"
"> “Adakah anda telah melancong ke mana-mana yang menarik baru-baru ini? "
"Saya melawat sebuah bandar kecil di tepi tasik hujung minggu lepas dan "
"sangat menyukainya.”\n"
"\n"
"Corak berguna adalah:\n"
"\n"
"**Tanya → Dengar → Respons → Kongsi → Tanya lagi**\n"
"\n"
"Ini mencipta perbualan seimbang di mana kedua-dua orang secara "
"beransur-ansur mendedahkan lebih banyak tentang diri mereka.\n"
"\n"
"## Cara Menarik Perbualan\n"
"\n"
"Dengar untuk butiran yang boleh anda terokai.\n"
"\n"
"Jika orang itu berkata:\n"
"\n"
"> “Saya baru-baru ini mula berlari.”\n"
"\n"
"Anda boleh bertanya:\n"
"\n"
"- “Apa yang membuat anda mula?”\n"
"- “Adakah anda lebih suka berlari sendirian atau dengan orang lain?”\n"
"- “Adakah sukar pada mulanya?”\n"
"- “Adakah anda berlatih untuk sesuatu?”\n"
"\n"
"Anda tidak perlu memperkenalkan topik yang benar-benar baru selepas setiap "
"jawapan. Seringkali, cara paling mudah untuk meneruskan adalah untuk "
"menjadi ingin tahu tentang satu butiran yang telah disebut oleh orang itu.\n"
"\n"
"## Apa Yang Perlu Dielakkan\n"
"\n"
"Cuba untuk tidak:\n"
"\n"
"- Tanya banyak soalan yang tidak berkaitan satu demi satu.\n"
"- Tukar setiap jawapan kembali kepada diri anda.\n"
"- Beri nasihat sebelum memahami apa yang orang perlukan.\n"
"- Tanya soalan yang terlalu peribadi terlalu cepat.\n"
"- Berpura-pura faham apabila anda keliru.\n"
"- Fokus terlalu banyak pada tatabahasa sempurna sehingga anda berhenti "
"mendengar.\n"
"\n"
"Adalah semula jadi sepenuhnya untuk berhenti seketika, mencari perkataan, "
"atau meminta seseorang untuk mengulangi diri mereka.\n"
"\n"
"Ungkapan berguna termasuk:\n"
"\n"
"- “Maaf, bolehkah anda katakan semula?”\n"
"- “Apa yang anda maksudkan dengan itu?”\n"
"- “Saya tidak pasti saya faham dengan betul.”\n"
"- “Bagaimana anda akan menerangkannya?”\n"
"- “Berikan saya satu saat—saya cuba mencari perkataan yang betul.”\n"
"\n"
"## Cara Menamatkan Perbualan Dengan Sopan\n"
"\n"
"Tidak setiap perbualan perlu berlangsung lama. Anda boleh selesai dengan "
"mesra tanpa menjadikan saat itu canggung:\n"
"\n"
"- “Sangat senang bercakap dengan anda.”\n"
"- “Saya akan dapatkan minuman lagi, tetapi saya gembira kita bertemu.”\n"
"- “Saya akan biarkan anda berbual dengan orang lain, tetapi saya seronok "
"dengan perbualan kita.”\n"
"- “Saya harap anda menikmati selebihnya acara ini.”\n"
"- “Mungkin saya akan berjumpa anda lagi nanti.”\n"
"\n"
"Menamatkan perbualan dengan sopan juga merupakan kemahiran komunikasi yang "
"penting.\n"
"\n"
"## Formula Perbualan Mudah\n"
"\n"
"Apabila anda tidak pasti apa yang perlu dilakukan, ingat:\n"
"\n"
"1. **Buka:** Komen tentang situasi yang dikongsi.\n"
"2. **Teroka:** Tanya tentang pengalaman, pilihan, atau perasaan.\n"
"3. **Dengar:** Respons kepada sesuatu yang spesifik yang mereka katakan.\n"
"4. **Hubung:** Kongsi maklumat yang berkaitan tentang diri anda.\n"
"5. **Teruskan atau tamatkan:** Tanya soalan susulan atau tamatkan dengan "
"sopan.\n"
"\n"
"## Senario Latihan\n"
"\n"
"Dalam permainan peranan ini, anda sedang berjumpa dengan seorang yang mesra "
"di acara sosial. Mulakan dengan soalan mudah, dengar butiran menarik, dan "
"secara beransur-ansur beralih dari fakta asas kepada pengalaman dan minat.\n"
"\n"
"Cuba untuk berlatih sekurang-kurangnya tiga kemahiran:\n"
"\n"
"- Tanya satu soalan tentang pengalaman atau perasaan.\n"
"- Rujuk kepada sesuatu yang telah dikatakan oleh orang asing itu "
"sebelumnya.\n"
"- Kongsi sesuatu yang berkaitan tentang diri anda.\n"
"\n"
"Jangan risau tentang mencipta perbualan yang sempurna. Tumpukan kepada "
"menjadi ingin tahu, perhatian, dan mudah untuk diajak berbual."

